#
# prima-materia — the Ra material, entered at The Law of One, Book I
#
# Opened from the structure-driven entrance of SPEC §14: pmt:RaMaterial was
# registered at pm:corpusNamed in traditions/registry-channeled.ttl with no
# node. The registration names the five books and the L/L Research session
# transcripts. What was opened is Book I, The Ra Material, in the L/L
# Research print of 1984: the introduction by Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty,
# the photographs and their captions, and sessions 1 to 26 (January 15 to
# February 17, 1981), read complete in a full-text layer of that edition.
# Books II to V are unopened and the work nodes say so.
#
# Order of the file: the works; the tradition with the three decisions; then
# the harvest in the order of the work, the introduction and sessions 1 to 8
# first, sessions 9 to 26 after, each session under its own heading.
#
# Citation. The questions are not numbered in this edition; nodes cite
# session, date and page. Page numbers stand at the foot of each page in the
# layer; missing and misread numerals were placed by sequence.
#
# Who speaks. A claim made by Ra is the work's claim. The introduction is by
# Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty and quotes earlier messages the group received
# from other contacts, chiefly one called Hatonn; their account of their own
# procedure and of earlier experiments is entered with the speaker named in
# the definition. A statement made only by the Questioner is entered only as a
# report of the group's own procedure or observation.
#
# Identifiers. Where the same term of the teaching is entered from both halves
# of the book, the node from sessions 9 to 26 carries the number of the session
# it starts from (pmc:RaHarvest and pmc:RaHarvestSession10): one doctrine, two
# places.
#

#
# The works
#

pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch I: Das Ra-Material"@de ;
    skos:note "Read complete on 2026-10-25 in The Law of One: Book I, The Ra Material, by Ra, An Humble Messenger of the Law of One, copyright 1984 by James Allen McCarty, Don Elkins and Carla Rueckert (Louisville: L/L Research), title page and copyright page in the full-text layer of archive.org the-ra-material-an-ancient-astronaut-speaks-by-don-elkins-james-allen-mc-carty-c, 500400 characters, ASCII letter share 1.0. The introduction (pp. 4-51), the photographs with their captions (pp. 52-68) and sessions 1 to 26 (pp. 70-233) were read complete in two halves, the introduction with sessions 1 to 8 and sessions 9 to 26, each by one reader writing the nodes from the wording. The library scan of the Donning print of 1984 (ramaterialancien00rasp) is lending-restricted and was not used."@en ;
    skos:note "The layer drops or misreads a number of page numerals, which were placed by sequence; the dates of sessions 9 and 10 read 'January tj' and are taken as January 27 from the sessions on either side; the text of footnote 3 on p. 232 is not in the layer. No stretch of running text is missing."@en ;
    skos:note "The book is the transcript of tape recordings of question and answer, and English is its original language, so the rule of two translations does not apply."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookTwo a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book II"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch II"@de ;
    skos:note "Sessions 27 to 50. Reachable: archive.org the-ra-material-the-law-of-one-v-1-5-don-elkins-carla-rueckert carries Books I to V in one full-text layer of about two million characters, without an imprint read. Not opened in this run, which took Book I complete instead of five books in part."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookThree a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book III"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch III"@de ;
    skos:note "Sessions 51 to 75. Reachable in the same full-text layer as Book II; not opened in this run."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFour a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book IV"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch IV"@de ;
    skos:note "Sessions 76 to 100. Reachable in the same full-text layer as Book II; not opened in this run. The registration places the examinable claims in the conditions of contact and the instrument's decline, which Books III to V carry at length."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFive a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book V: Personal Material"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch V: Persönliches Material"@de ;
    skos:note "The fragments withheld from Books I to IV, with commentary by Rueckert and McCarty. Reachable in the same full-text layer as Book II; not opened in this run."@en .

#
# The tradition
#

pmt:RaMaterial a pm:Tradition ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    rdfs:label "The Ra material"@en, "Das Ra-Material"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transmission of one hundred and six sessions received between 1981 and 1984 by a group of three working in fixed roles, teaching a cosmology of densities, a choice between service to others and service to self, and a harvest at the close of a cycle."@en ;
    skos:note "The best documented reception in the block. Questioner, instrument and scribe are named, the sessions are numbered and dated, the working conditions are described including the instrument's physical decline, and the transmission continued under a different contact after this one ended. The cosmological claims are largely undecidable; the claims about the conditions of contact and about what the work cost the instrument are not, and that is where an examination would begin."@en ;
    skos:note "Contact route, the first of the three decisions SPEC §14 requires, kept at documented, and the route is printed in the work. The introduction describes nineteen years of the group's meditation and channelling before Ra, after the method of an earlier contactee group, with messages from a contact called Hatonn of the same Confederation that Ra names; Elkins sets his account in the physics of Dewey Larson; and when the Questioner reads out Oahspe's figure of fifty-one per cent service to others for harvest, Ra calls it correct. Agreement of this material with the contactee literature, with Theosophy or with Oahspe is reception along that route and counts once."@en ;
    skos:note "Recension and edition, the second decision: Book I in the L/L Research print of 1984, the transcript the group itself published, cited by session, date and page. The tapes and the later relistened transcripts of L/L Research were not compared; where a later edition corrects a word, the node does not know it."@en ;
    skos:note "The third decision, the number of citable places: Book I read complete, 368 nodes in the order of the work, 187 from the introduction and sessions 1 to 8 and 181 from sessions 9 to 26, each at a session and page."@en ;
    skos:note "Two counts, kept apart as SPEC §15 asks. Signs of success: twenty, eleven of them from the introduction (the reception of the group's channels, the bending of metal, psychic surgery, meditation) and nine from Ra (among them a life span near nine hundred years as the mark of a harmonious people, the feeling of being awakened in a wanderer, hope and friendly feeling as the marks of a positive contact). Conditions of failure: sixty-one. Twelve set a deadline, threshold or count: the 51 and 5 per cent of harvest, the 25,000-year cycle that strikes like a clock, an approximate harvest in 2011, life spans falling from 900 to 35-40 years, misalignments of the instrument's articles by 3, 1.4, 0.5 and 0.2 degrees, two sessions a day found too wearing. Forty-one name an outcome someone could notice. Where the failure is put: on the instrument thirteen times, on the hearer's free will ten, on the seeker's own orientation and practice and on the researcher's attitude most of the rest, on the Questioner's questions once, and never on discord in the group."@en ;
    skos:note "The finding the count carries. Three of the introduction's conditions of failure announce in advance that the phenomena will not appear under examination: desire for proof, rigorous controls and the analysis of specimens are each said to dampen or annul the effect (pmc:RaProofNullResults, pmc:RaRigorousControlsDampen, pmc:RaSpecimenAnalysisCaution). Ra's own observable failures in sessions 1 to 8 lie almost wholly on the instrument's body and the arrangement of the room, which is the examinable layer the registration pointed at. And the one disagreement inside the book is of that kind: Ra says the instrument can sustain two sessions a day, the introduction reports that two a day proved much too wearing (pmc:RaTwoSessionsDispute)."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty, The Law of One, Books I to V; the L/L Research session transcripts" ;
    pm:corpusWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookTwo, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookThree, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFour, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFive ;
    pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 4-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .


#
# Introduction (Elkins, Rueckert, McCarty), pp. 4-51
#

pmc:RaContactReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The work's claim that its wording is Ra's, spoken through Carla Rueckert in trance"@en, "Die Behauptung des Werkes, sein Wortlaut sei der Ras, gesprochen durch Carla Rueckert in Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "The claim the book makes about its own authorship. Elkins calls it an exact transcript from tape recordings of twenty-six sessions of an experiment designed to communicate with an extraterrestrial being, the race called Ra, by what he prefers to call tuned trance telepathy. The prefatory note to the sessions says the group began receiving a communication from the social memory complex Ra on January 15, 1981, and that the pages contain an exact transcript of the first twenty-six sessions, edited only to remove some personal material."@en ;
    skos:note "This node records the claim, not its truth. The title page names Ra as author, an humble messenger of the Law of One, and the copyright holders as McCarty, Elkins and Rueckert; the source lines here name the edition a reader can obtain. Rueckert says she does not know how the trance occurs, and Elkins classes her state as telepathic reception in the trance state."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Carla L. Rueckert, the instrument, in trance; questions asked by Don Elkins, the questioner; transcription by James Allen McCarty" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Ra, which calls itself a social memory complex of those who are of the Law of One and an humble messenger of the Law of One; called by Elkins a sixth-density social memory complex" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "The contact began on January 15, 1981, three weeks after McCarty joined the group and a few days after Rueckert's first experience of trance, two sittings to contact a deceased friend. It came while she was working with an advanced meditation student, Leonard Cecil; she challenged the entity in the name of Christ, it remained, and she went almost immediately into trance. Before each session the group decided the night before, gave the instrument a half-hour back massage, meditated, performed a ritual of protection and cleansing of the room, laid her prone under a white blanket with her eyes covered and hooked up three tape recorder microphones below her chin; Elkins aligned the table bearing Bible, candle, incense and chalice of water with her head, and Elkins and McCarty walked the Circle of One. McCarty says she departs her physical body and Ra uses it to make the words; she has no memory of the session; Elkins calls her name until she responds. McCarty transcribed the tapes. The questions were prepared by all three and asked by Elkins." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 4-5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 47-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), prefatory note to the sessions, p. 69; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaTunedTranceTelepathy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tuned trance telepathy: Elkins's name for the group's method of contact"@en, "Abgestimmte Trance-Telepathie: Elkins' Name für die Kontaktmethode der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins says the research group uses what he prefers to call tuned trance telepathy to communicate with an extraterrestrial race called Ra, in English because Ra knows it. Rueckert reports that Elkins, though he finds her trance similar to others he has observed, calls it telepathic reception in the trance state, and that neither she nor the others know how to aid her beyond a certain point in achieving it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHoaxCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Extreme caution before concluding: hoaxes and garbage data in paranormal research"@en, "Äußerste Vorsicht vor Schlüssen: Schwindel und Datenmüll in der paranormalen Forschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins, after almost thirty years of research in so-called paranormal phenomena, recommends extreme caution in reaching a conclusion. Where it is possible to make money, gain notoriety or have fun by perpetrating a hoax, someone usually does it; paranormal and psychic areas are therefore prime targets for the trickster, and the careful researcher usually has to observe copious amounts of garbage data to find a possible imbedded gem of truth, especially in Philippine psychic surgery and in spirit communication in general. He says the book is not a treatise of his opinion, that his opinion may change at any time, and that only time will tell the accuracy of his best guess."@en ;
    skos:note "A caution the editors direct at their own field, including the channelling the book consists of."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaTunedTranceTelepathy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 4-5; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaVocalChanneling a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Vocal channelling: speaking the thoughts that come and analysing only afterwards"@en, "Stimmliches Channeln: die kommenden Gedanken aussprechen und erst danach prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The group sat meditating according to instructions in material Harold Price had brought from a Detroit group, which gave the means of generating further material from the same source without physical contact. Through the Detroit contactee Walter Rogers the group was instructed to refrain from analysis, to speak the thoughts, and to analyze the communication only after it had been completed. Rueckert describes her own practice as conscious channelling, using her free will to clothe telepathic concepts in her own language; in free will channelling one can choose to stop, and the channel never knows in advance what the next concept will be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 48-49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTelepathicReception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reception of transmissions by telepathic contact"@en, "Empfang von Übermittlungen durch telepathischen Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to receive transmissions, that is, to produce information by telepathic contact with a source held to be extraterrestrial, which the introduction reports for the members of Elkins's experimental group from 1962 and for receivers trained in later meetings. Hatonn, quoted in the introduction, says that those who receive the passed-on information will themselves be able to reach a state of thinking sufficiently in tune with the Confederation's vibrations to receive its contact, so that the process is self-generating."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 8; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVocalChannelingYieldsReception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking the thoughts without analysis yields reception within a month for half the group"@en, "Das Aussprechen der Gedanken ohne Prüfung bringt binnen eines Monats der halben Gruppe den Empfang"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the night the group was told to speak its thoughts, a month had not gone by before half the group had begun to produce information, and within a year all in the group except Rueckert were able to receive transmissions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: half the group producing information within a month and all but one receiving within a year, a count the introduction gives itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaFearOfImproperWords a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of not speaking the proper words blocks the instrument and slows the speech"@en, "Die Furcht, nicht die rechten Worte zu sprechen, blockiert das Instrument und verlangsamt die Rede"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the first six months, sitting meditating according to the instructions, everyone in the group except Rueckert made only strange noises with their mouths, guttural clicks, slurps and tongue flops. The visiting contactee was then told by telepathic impression that the members were being used as instruments of communication but were all blocked through fear that they would not be speaking the proper words. After the block was lifted the speech was slow and difficult at first, because each receiver wanted a precise impression of each and every word and in many cases wanted to be completely controlled for fear of making an error in transmission."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the fear of the wrong word is named as the block, and the wish for complete control as the cause of the slow speech; the outcomes, noises without words and then slow speech, are observable, and the failure is put on the instruments."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaProofNullResults a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A desire for proof leads to null results and voided experiments"@en, "Ein Verlangen nach Beweis führt zu Nullergebnissen und ungültigen Versuchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert says Elkins counts her great gullibility among her assets as a research associate: she takes things at face value and analyzes only afterwards, and she calls this a vital factor in obtaining good results in paranormal research. A desire for proof will inevitably lead to null results and voided experiments. An open mind, one willing to be gullible, leads to a subjective and personal certainty which does not equal proof, as it cannot be systematically reproduced in others; she calls this subjective knowing a central part of the spiritual evolution Ra speaks of."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the researcher's desire for proof is named as what produces null results; the outcome is observable, the cause is an attitude of the researcher. The same passage warns the reader that the certainty it offers is not proof."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaTunedTranceTelepathy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 7; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMaterializationMediumship a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Materialization of spirits in a seance"@en, "Materialisation von Geistern in einer Séance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert reports four demonstrations by the Spiritualist minister James Tingley in Toledo in 1971, whose concrete-block meeting place Elkins had examined inside and out and found without gadgets: ghost-like figures seen clearly, Elkins seeing even the strands of hair; a solid ghost known as Sister, whom Elkins later linked to his mother; and a Master who made the room grow very cold, touched Rueckert hard enough to bruise her arm so that she would know he was real, walked through the two of them, blessed the room, and pooled down on the floor and was gone. Elkins had sought such a materialization, one he himself could believe, because he thought seance materializations might be of the same nature as those of UFOs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 7-8; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaDailyMentalTuning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Daily meetings for intensive mental tuning"@en, "Tägliche Treffen zur intensiven geistigen Abstimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "From 1974, after twelve years of listening, Elkins had Rueckert take up channelling seriously, and the two began a series of daily meetings designed to work intensively on her mental tuning; others from the Sunday night meditations joined them. During these intensive meditations the group began keeping the tape recorder going whenever a session started."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 8; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDailyMentalTuningYieldsReception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Daily intensive meditation yields about a dozen new receivers in three months"@en, "Tägliche intensive Meditation bringt in drei Monaten etwa ein Dutzend neue Empfänger hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within three months of the daily meetings the group generated about a dozen new telepathic receivers."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: about a dozen new receivers within three months."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaDailyMentalTuning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 8; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaHypnoticRegression a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Regressive hypnosis: age regression, lost time and previous lives"@en, "Regressive Hypnose: Altersregression, verlorene Zeit und frühere Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regressive hypnosis as the group used it: Elkins's more than two hundred age regressions probing past the birth experience; the regression of UFO witnesses to recover the time they could not account for, after a lengthy induction to the proper state of concentration; and the separate regression of four subjects to a life on another planet, questioned by Elkins and the hypnotist Lawrence Allison."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 10-11; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 36-42; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPastLifeRecall a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recall under hypnosis of lost time and of previous incarnations"@en, "Erinnerung unter Hypnose an verlorene Zeit und frühere Inkarnationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recall under hypnosis of what the conscious mind does not hold. The introduction reports a nineteen-year-old who recovered thirty-eight lost minutes as an examination aboard a craft by three machine-like beings; Elkins's early investigations, which seemed to indicate that reincarnation was a probability and that incarnations contain situations and lessons more easily understood in the light of previous incarnations; and three women and one man who, separately regressed, gave independent and dovetailing accounts of one community on another planet, a temple, wordless communication and a life of study and meditation, the man adding technical detail."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 10-11; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 19; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 36-42; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHypnoticRegressionYieldsRecall a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Regressive hypnosis yields recall of lost time and previous lives"@en, "Regressive Hypnose bringt die Erinnerung an verlorene Zeit und frühere Leben hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The witness who wished to find his lost time was moved back under hypnosis to the moment beneath the craft and found himself inside it; the four subjects regressed to the other planet described its clothing, its temple, its music and its manner of speaking without words, and the man was brought through his death there and paused between incarnations to say why he had come to Earth: to help the people who are lost."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaHypnoticRegression ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPastLifeRecall ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 10-11; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 36-42; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRigorousControlsDampen a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Rigorous controls dampen the outcome of telepathic experiments"@en, "Strenge Kontrollen dämpfen den Ausgang telepathischer Versuche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction says there has never been a definitive study proving good telepathic communication. Elkins states that his telepathic experiments with Uri Geller have been totally successful, but that they were deliberately not performed under rigorous scientific control and could not be included in any orthodox report; the authors give it as their opinion that rigorous controls have a dampening effect on the outcome of any experiment of this type. They keep the word alleged before telepathic communications from extraterrestrials because there is no way of proving the basic concept."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: controls are named as what dampens the outcome, so that a null result under control is announced in advance as an effect of the control rather than of the claim; the failure is put on the experimental conditions. The introduction later cites John Taylor's controlled experiments with children as good solid data (p. 18), so the authors hold both positions; one voice, not entered as a dispute."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 11-12; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMetalBendingByWanting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling metal to bend without touching it forcefully"@en, "Metall heißen, sich zu biegen, ohne es kräftig zu berühren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins, on the telephone with a fourteen-year-old who had had a UFO encounter, asked him to take a piece of silverware and tell it to bend without touching it in any firm or forceful way. The introduction also reports children who, after watching Uri Geller on television, cause bends and breaks in metal and other materials just by wanting the break or bend to occur."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 12; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMentalMetalBending a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Action at a distance by the mind: bending and breaking metal by wanting it"@en, "Fernwirkung durch den Geist: Metall durch Wollen biegen und brechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Action at a distance as a function of mind, specifically the will, which the introduction says the physics Ra discusses posits: the bending and breaking of metal and plastic objects without force, done mostly by children and increasing in number daily, including objects sealed in glass cylinders by a glass blower in John Taylor's experiments with about fifty children. Rueckert says the reader of the Ra material will discover why it is mostly children who can do this and what it has to do with the rest of the UFO message."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 12-13; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMetalBendingYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Telling the fork to bend yields the bend"@en, "Die Gabel heißen, sich zu biegen, bringt die Biegung hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The boy picked up a fork, did as Elkins suggested, and the fork immediately bent nearly double; he was so startled that he would not come back to the telephone. Under Taylor's controlled circumstances the children were still able to bend and break multitudinous objects."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the fork bent nearly double at once; under seal, the objects bent and broke."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMetalBendingByWanting ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaMentalMetalBending ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 12-13; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaHigherSelfInquiry a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking the Higher Self under hypnosis whether the lesson is learned"@en, "Das höhere Selbst unter Hypnose fragen, ob die Lektion gelernt ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a previous life had been discussed and while the subject was still in trance, the hypnotist Lawrence Allison asked him, as he often did, to contact what is loosely referred to as his Higher Self, and had him ask whether the lesson of that life had been learned and whether, since it had, the symptom tied to it could be healed as no longer necessary."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 19; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHigherSelfNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Higher Self, consulted under hypnosis"@en, "Das höhere Selbst, unter Hypnose befragt"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the hypnotist loosely calls the subject's Higher Self is asked through the subject in trance and answers: it says the lesson has been learned and agrees that the allergy may be healed."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Higher Self" ;
    pm:nameRole "the subject's own higher self, reached through the subject under hypnosis and able to judge whether a lesson is learned and to consent to a healing" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 19; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLessonLearning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lessons chosen before incarnation, to be learned and not avoided"@en, "Vor der Inkarnation gewählte Lektionen, zu lernen und nicht zu umgehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn, quoted in the introduction, says that at incarnation each was aware that certain lessons hitherto unlearned were to be the goals of this incarnation; a life that seems a series of difficulties of one particular type points to one of them; they are not to be avoided but learned. Rueckert says the lessons are always along the lines of how to love better, more fully, more deeply or with more kindness, and that each entity's are unique; the introduction's allergy case speaks of the lesson of putting people first."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 31-32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHigherSelfHealing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing of a condition whose lesson has been learned, by the Higher Self's consent"@en, "Heilung eines Leidens, dessen Lektion gelernt ist, mit Zustimmung des höheren Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "A boy whose allergies to all living things kept him from cutting grass, smelling flowers or going outside in the blooming season was regressed to a life as a solitary English landowner who avoided all human contact and whose one pleasure was his garden. His Higher Self said the lesson of putting people first had been learned and agreed that the allergy could be healed, since it was no longer necessary. Rueckert gives it as an example of the relationship some call karma."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHigherSelfInquiryYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Asking the Higher Self yields the cure of the allergy"@en, "Die Befragung des höheren Selbst bringt die Heilung der Allergie hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hypnotist brought the boy out of trance, scraped magnolia pollen from his piano and blew it directly at the boy's nose. The boy protested that he was allergic; the hypnotist answered that he did not hear him sneezing. The boy remained cured of his allergy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: no sneeze at the pollen, and the cure lasting."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaHigherSelfInquiry ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaHigherSelfHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLessonBeforeHealing a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The lesson learned before the symptom is healed"@en, "Die Lektion gelernt, bevor das Symptom geheilt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "The healing was asked for on the ground that the lesson had been learned and the allergy was therefore no longer necessary; the Higher Self was asked first whether the lesson had been learned and only then whether the allergy could be healed."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order and not stated necessity: the account gives the learned lesson as the reason for the healing and does not say what happens when the healing is asked for first."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaHigherSelfHealing ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaLessonLearning ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMagicalPersonalityWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Work upon the magical personality: interiorizing, accepting responsibility, balancing reactions"@en, "Arbeit an der magischen Persönlichkeit: verinnerlichen, Verantwortung übernehmen, Reaktionen ausgleichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert describes a study of the so-called magical personality: by interiorizing experience, by accepting responsibility for all that occurs, by carefully analyzing one's reactions to all that occurs, and by eventually balancing those reactions so that one's actions are generated within the self and are no longer simple reactions to outward stimulus. Each time a person sustains an unfortunate situation and reacts by not giving anger for anger or sadness for sadness but by offering compassion and comfort where none was expected, the thread of inner strength is strengthened."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMagicalPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The magical personality and the art of causing changes in consciousness at will"@en, "Die magische Persönlichkeit und die Kunst, Veränderungen des Bewusstseins nach Willen zu bewirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "A thread that runs through daily life which can be grasped and used to remove oneself from time to time into a framework in which reality is seen as that of the spiritual body, the personality that exists from incarnation to incarnation. Strengthened, it gives some small claim to the art of causing changes in consciousness at will, which Rueckert calls the classic definition of magic, and associates one more and more with a life closely related to the organic evolution of the universe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMagicalPersonalityWorkYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Work upon the magical personality yields a small claim to magic"@en, "Die Arbeit an der magischen Persönlichkeit bringt einen kleinen Anspruch auf Magie hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "By working upon the magical personality in these ways we strengthen it until we are able to have some small claim to the art of causing changes in consciousness at will."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMagicalPersonalityWork ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaMagicalPersonality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHatonnReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The introduction's claim that its quoted messages come from Hatonn through the group's channels"@en, "Die Behauptung der Einleitung, ihre zitierten Botschaften stammten von Hatonn durch die Kanäle der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction quotes at length messages received in the group's meetings and attributes them to an entity called Hatonn, of the Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator, who has spoken with the group and several others for many years."@en ;
    skos:note "The receiver is deliberately unnamed, which is itself a finding about this witness: the shape asks for the person through whom the wording came, and the work withholds it on principle. One quoted passage says my voice is now the voice of this instrument, my thoughts are her thoughts, so at least that receiver was a woman."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "unnamed vocal channels of the Louisville meditation group; the introduction says the group never describes who the receiver was" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Hatonn, of the Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator, speaking from a craft above the group" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Messages received in the group's meditation meetings, held in Louisville since 1962 and taped since 1974, through members trained as vocal channels; the introduction quotes transcripts and marks breaks between transcripts with a symbol, and gives as its reason for naming no receiver that the information matters rather than the person transmitting." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHatonnNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Hatonn, a Confederation entity speaking through the group"@en, "Hatonn, ein Wesen der Konföderation, das durch die Gruppe spricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "An entity called Hatonn, who has spoken with the group and several others for many years, says that the purpose of at least some of the UFOs seen at this time is a desire to be of service, that he is in a craft far above the group's dwelling and able to monitor its thoughts, which the Confederation does not consider an infringement since it sees these thoughts as its own and as the Creator's, and that the Confederation are the Harvesters."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Hatonn" ;
    pm:nameRole "a member entity of the Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator, in a craft above the Earth, speaking through vocal channels" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaConfederation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator"@en, "Die Konföderation der Planeten im Dienst des Unendlichen Schöpfers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The name used by Hatonn and by Ra. Ra counts approximately fifty-three civilizations comprising approximately five hundred planetary consciousness complexes, among them those from this planet who have attained dimensions beyond the third, planetary entities within this solar system and planetary entities from other galaxies; a true confederation in that its members are not alike but allied in service according to the Law of One. Its members wait for the calling. Hatonn says they have contacted the people of Earth at intervals of thousands of years, those who sought their aid, and are very sorry they cannot step upon the soil and teach."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 101-102; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVibratoryRate a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The vibration or vibratory rate of the individual"@en, "Die Schwingung oder Schwingungsrate des Einzelnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says that the receiver must become of a certain vibration as a result of his thinking, that the channels' verbal communications create a system of thought and a desire for spiritual awareness that raises his vibration, and that the choice each person makes is measured by his vibratory rate, which motivation from within increases and proof imposed from without does not."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 34-35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVibrationBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A certain vibration first, then contact: raised by thinking, speeded by groups, finished in meditation"@en, "Erst eine bestimmte Schwingung, dann der Kontakt: durch Denken gehoben, durch Gruppen beschleunigt, in der Meditation vollendet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: for this is how contacts work. It is first necessary, if the entity is to be able to receive our contact, for him to become of a certain vibration as a result of his thinking. This is greatly speeded by involvement in groups such as this, and it is finally done through meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a receiver who has not reached the vibration cannot receive the contact; no threshold is given and the failure is put on the receiver's thinking."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaVibratoryRate ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The entity is not able to receive the contact: it is first necessary, if the entity is to be able to receive our contact, for him to become of a certain vibration." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTruthWithoutProof a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Truth offered without proof: imposed or proven, it would have no usable effect"@en, "Wahrheit ohne Beweis angeboten: aufgezwungen oder bewiesen, hätte sie keine brauchbare Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says the Confederation cannot step upon the soil and teach, for this would be a very great disservice to those who do not desire its service, and would have little effect even on those who desire it, since understanding comes from within; its very utterance would be accepted by many as valid, and it does not wish to be thought the ultimate representative of the Creator's truth. Truth must be realized from within and cannot be impressed from without; the Confederation remains in hiding because it cannot serve one individual and at the same time do a disservice to his neighbour by proving within his own mind that it exists. It offers truth without proof, so that the motivation comes from within and the vibratory rate is increased; an offering of proof, or an impressing of truth such that one would be forced to accept it, would have no usable effect upon his vibratory rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: forced acceptance and proof are named as having no usable effect on the vibratory rate; the outcome is not observable, and the failure is put on the hearer's free will. A caution that also explains in advance why no proof will be given."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaVibratoryRate ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 28; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaOriginalThought a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The original thought: love as the unity in which each sees the other as the Creator"@en, "Der ursprüngliche Gedanke: Liebe als die Einheit, in der jeder den anderen als den Schöpfer sieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "What members of the Confederation call the original thought, which Rueckert glosses as love implying a unity so great that we see each other and ourselves as the Creator and so see one being; she calls it the very heart of telepathy. Hatonn says all thought that is generated is generated by the Creator, whose infinite parts all have free will, and that man on Earth has become isolated in his thinking from the concept that permeates most of the creation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 23-24; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation as the Confederation messages ask for it"@en, "Meditation, wie die Botschaften der Konföderation sie verlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meditation, always suggested in the contactee messages as the best means of attaining understanding, of progressing spiritually and of understanding the nature and purpose of the illusion. Hatonn says it stills the active conscious mind, which is continually seeking stimulus within the illusion; that it begins as a simple process and little by little becomes a way in which one lives; and that the Confederation cannot overemphasize its importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the introduction says the seeker's state of mind has the opportunity of being continuously in a far more pleasant configuration than that of one not seeking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 25-27; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 29-30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAppreciationOfReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Appreciation of reality: the illusion of separation reduced to a total illusion"@en, "Wertschätzung der Wirklichkeit: die Illusion der Trennung auf eine völlige Illusion zurückgeführt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The return to an appreciation of reality, of the functioning of the real creation, rather than of the illusion created by man's mind; Hatonn says man on Earth has lost this awareness because he has focused on devices and inventions of his own and become hypnotized by his playthings and ideas, and that through meditation it is possible totally to reduce the illusion that creates the separation to what it actually is, a total illusion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 25-26; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsAppreciationOfReality a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation yields, very rapidly, the return to an appreciation of reality"@en, "Meditation bringt sehr rasch die Rückkehr zur Wertschätzung der Wirklichkeit hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: all of this may be very simply remedied. All that is necessary is that he individually avail himself to this appreciation of reality through the process of meditation, for this process stills his active conscious mind; very rapidly, then, he can return to an appreciation of the reality in the functioning of the real creation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaAppreciationOfReality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaIllusion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The illusion: physical existence as a teaching that teaches only those aware of it"@en, "Die Illusion: das physische Dasein als eine Lehre, die nur lehrt, wer sie bemerkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The day-to-day physical existence, which the Confederation calls an illusion. Hatonn says man on Earth generated it out of desire; that it is very useful for those who wish to evolve rapidly by experiencing and using it, so that many Confederation members would desire the opportunity to be within it; that it surrounds one for the purpose of teaching and can only teach if one becomes aware of its teachings; that many souls experience it and few use it to grow; and that once one is aware of the possibility, it is necessary to take the next step and express, regardless of the potentials which affect one, the love and understanding of the Creator, as the teacher known as Jesus did."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 26-27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRealDesire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of one's real desire, which is the Creator's desire, Love"@en, "Das Gewahrsein des eigenen wirklichen Verlangens, das das Verlangen des Schöpfers ist, die Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn states without exception that man receives exactly what he desires, though it seems otherwise; perhaps desire is not understood, and the understanding is not within the intellectual mind; it may be necessary to spend time in meditation to become aware of one's real desire. When one knows the Creator's desire one knows one's own, for one is one with the Creator and all His parts; that desire is that all His parts express and experience the Love that created them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsRealDesire a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation yields the knowledge of the Creator's desire, and with it the end of questions"@en, "Meditation bringt die Kenntnis des Verlangens des Schöpfers hervor, und mit ihr das Ende der Fragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: become aware of your Creator and of His desire; when you know His desire you will feel it; there will be no more confusion, there will be no more questions, you will have found what you have sought; you will have found Love. This may be found simply, in meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: felt knowledge, the end of confusion and of questions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaRealDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaIntellectualSeekingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No interpretation of the written or spoken word will lead to the simple truth"@en, "Keine Auslegung des geschriebenen oder gesprochenen Wortes führt zur einfachen Wahrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: no amount of seeking within the intellectual concepts of your people, no amount of careful planning or careful interpretation of the written or spoken word will lead you to the simple truth; it may be found simply, in meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning: the book consists of written words of this kind, and the caution, quoted by the editors, places its own reading below meditation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContactReceiving ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLawOfConfusion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of Confusion, called the Law of Free Will"@en, "Das Gesetz der Verwirrung, Gesetz des freien Willens genannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra calls the Law of Confusion, which the questioner has called the Law of Free Will, one of the more significant primal distortions of the Law of One. The introduction says the Confederation holds free will to be at the foundation of the universe, each entity a totally unique part of the one unity, and that its concern is always to avoid infringement upon the free will of any person, which shapes its method of contact. Ra says those who found the light/love of a density without desire for service to others have by the Law of Free Will the right to its use for whatever purpose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 28; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), pp. 84-85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaWisdomCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Be careful of what you know: in the real creation it has power, and desire aims it"@en, "Hütet euch vor dem, was ihr wisst: in der wirklichen Schöpfung hat es Macht, und das Verlangen richtet sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: there are pieces of information that are of importance and pieces that are not. Wisdom is a rather lonely matter, and you must accept this as you acquire the burden of wisdom. That which you know, you are to be careful of, for what you know in the real creation has power, and that which you desire is all of the direction at which that power will be aimed; but have faith in what you know and feed your faith and understanding through meditation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 29; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaServiceToOthers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Service to others, which is service to self"@en, "Dienst an anderen, der Dienst am Selbst ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says service to others is service to one's self, not alike but identical, since there is identity between others and ourselves, and that each person is a completely free entity whose independence must in no way be shaken. Ra says that to serve one is to serve all; that service to others results in service to self, preserving and further harmonizing the distortions of those seeking intelligent infinity through these disciplines; and that the Confederation waits for the calling."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 73; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 108; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaNegativityInService a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A negative feeling toward another stains the service one gives"@en, "Ein negatives Gefühl gegenüber einem anderen befleckt den Dienst, den man leistet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: that which is felt of a negative nature towards a sheep of the flock is felt towards one's self and towards the Creator; this enters the service one attempts to give to oneself and to the Creator through service to another and causes a blot or a stain upon the perfect service one would have performed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the negative feeling is named as what spoils the service; the outcome is not observable and the failure is put on the server's own feeling."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaServiceToOthers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaReadinessToServe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Readiness to serve: answers to all one's questions, received in meditation"@en, "Bereitschaft zum Dienst: Antworten auf alle Fragen, in der Meditation empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn names one thing of great importance, personal preparation for the service of one's fellow man. Through meditation one will receive answers to all one's questions, which can be reduced to an extremely simple concept; once this has been done one will be ready to serve, as others have served, qualified to reach out to one's fellow man and lead him from the darkness of confusion back into the light that he desires."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsReadinessToServe a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation yields the preparation for service"@en, "Meditation bringt die Vorbereitung zum Dienst hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: it is necessary that you prepare yourselves for this service. This of course is done in meditation; through this technique you will receive answers to all of your questions; once this has been done you will be ready to serve."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaReadinessToServe ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaProficientVocalChannel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Proficiency as a vocal channel who receives the Confederation's thoughts readily"@en, "Gewandtheit als stimmlicher Kanal, der die Gedanken der Konföderation leicht empfängt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says there is a need for many more channels who can receive directly the thoughts so many people are seeking, and that the Confederation is attempting to generate greater numbers of proficient vocal channels who can receive its thoughts quite readily. Rueckert says the Confederation sources greatly appreciate vocal channels trained in groups such as the one in Louisville since 1962, never suggest their message is unique, and can only perform their service through vocal channels."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 30-31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDailyMeditationYieldsChannel a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Daily meditation, with the desire for contact, is all that is required for a vocal channel"@en, "Tägliche Meditation, mit dem Verlangen nach Kontakt, ist alles, was ein stimmlicher Kanal braucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: this requires daily meditation. This is all that is required: daily meditation. It is assumed, of course, that as this daily meditation is performed there is a desire for our contact."@en ;
    skos:note "The only sufficiency statement in the part: one practice and one assumed desire are said to be all that is required, which makes a meditator with the desire who does not become a proficient channel a case against it. The text names no period."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaProficientVocalChannel ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSoloContactCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not to attempt Confederation contact in solitary meditation, only in a group with an experienced receiver"@en, "Keinen Kontakt zur Konföderation in einsamer Meditation versuchen, nur in einer Gruppe mit einem erfahrenen Empfänger"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert, as one who has participated in meditation groups for many years, suggests that individual meditations not include the attempt to contact Confederation sources; it is best to pursue the attempt only in a group situation, preferably a group which contains at least one experienced receiver."@en ;
    skos:note "No reason and no consequence is given; the caution is a recommendation from experience."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaTuning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tuning before meditation: prayer, chanting, inspirational reading or the white light"@en, "Abstimmung vor der Meditation: Gebet, Gesang, erbauliche Lektüre oder das weiße Licht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert strongly recommends, whether meditating alone or in a group, some means of tuning so that the meditation which follows will be at the highest spiritual level possible. It can be done in any way preferable to the meditator: the Lord's Prayer, Aum-ing or other singing or chanting, the reading of some inspirational writing, or a careful visualization of the white light of the Creator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTunedState a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The tuned state: meditation at its highest level, the instrument precisely tuned"@en, "Der abgestimmte Zustand: Meditation auf ihrer höchsten Stufe, das Instrument genau abgestimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the meditator, the state in which the meditation is at the highest spiritual level possible. For the instrument, the precise tuning Ra says it had to wait for before speaking through her, because it sends a narrow band vibration, and the proper state of depth of singleness or one-pointedness it waited for again before answering a question."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 70; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 72; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTuningYieldsTunedState a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tuning yields meditation at the highest spiritual level possible"@en, "Abstimmung bringt Meditation auf der höchsten möglichen geistigen Stufe hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The tuning is recommended so that the meditation which follows will be at the highest spiritual level possible."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaTuning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaTunedState ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaForgettingProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The forgetting process at birth into this incarnation"@en, "Der Vorgang des Vergessens bei der Geburt in diese Inkarnation"@de ;
    skos:definition "What Ra calls the forgetting process, which occurs at the time of birth into this incarnation and veils the lessons one came to learn; for a Wanderer, the love and the light the person was intended to share."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 36; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPenetratingTheForgetting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Penetrating the forgetting process and becoming aware of one's lessons"@en, "Den Vorgang des Vergessens durchdringen und der eigenen Lektionen gewahr werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of the most highly regarded fruits of meditation and seeking, the introduction says: the ability of the seeker to penetrate the forgetting process so as to become aware of the lessons to be learned during this incarnation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsPenetratingTheForgetting a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation and seeking yield the penetration of the forgetting process"@en, "Meditation und Suchen bringen das Durchdringen des Vergessens hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction counts among the most highly regarded fruits of the meditation and seeking process the ability to penetrate the forgetting process that occurs at birth."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPenetratingTheForgetting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAnalyticalAvoidance a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "One's own thinking helps one avoid the lesson one wishes to learn"@en, "Das eigene Denken hilft, die Lektion zu umgehen, die man lernen will"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: when a confrontation in such a lesson has been achieved, that which separates you from understanding is most often your own thinking. Your conscious thinking processes are quite capable of being self-destructive in the sense that they may aid you to avoid the lesson you wish in reality to learn. If a temporary abeyance of the conscious, analytical processes can be achieved, you may return to the problem with a much clearer mentality, ready to learn rather than only to avoid what you came to learn."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the lesson is not learned because analytical thought avoids it; the failure is put on the seeker's own thinking and is recognized by the repetition of the difficulty."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaLessonLearning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 31-32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaSemiMeditativeState a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal meditation, then a semi-meditative state of attention at all times"@en, "Förmliche Meditation, dann jederzeit ein halbmeditativer Zustand der Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn, knowing how difficult it is to achieve the meditative state at all times, urges dependence on meditation of a formal kind and then the attempt at a semi-meditative state at all times, by which he means simply a state of attention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSemiMeditativeStateYieldsLessons a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The semi-meditative state keeps destructive impulses from blocking the lessons"@en, "Der halbmeditative Zustand hält zerstörerische Regungen davon ab, die Lektionen zu verstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state of attention is to be kept so that one's destructive impulses are not free to clog the mind completely and keep one from learning the lessons one came to learn."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaSemiMeditativeState ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaLessonLearning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMeditationOnUnity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditating upon the complete unity of oneself and all one sees, especially in difficulty"@en, "Über die vollständige Einheit des Selbst mit allem Gesehenen meditieren, besonders in Schwierigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: meditate upon the complete unity of yourself and all that you see; do this not once, and not simply in present circumstances, but at all times, and especially in difficult circumstances; keep your mind stayed upon the unity of the Creator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAlleviationByUnity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alleviation of difficult circumstances by loving and feeling at one with them"@en, "Linderung schwieriger Umstände, indem man sie liebt und sich eins mit ihnen fühlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Insofar as one loves and feels at one with the things that are difficult, to that extent those circumstances are alleviated. Hatonn attributes this not to any law within the physical illusion but to the Law of Love: the spiritual body, interpenetrated with the physical body, is higher than it, and the changes one makes by love upon the spiritual body of necessity reflect themselves within the physical illusion. Even if the universe of those around remains disharmonious, one's own universe will become harmonious, not by one's own doing but by the love of the Creator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationOnUnityYieldsAlleviation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation on unity yields the alleviation of difficult circumstances"@en, "Meditation über die Einheit bringt die Linderung schwieriger Umstände hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: insofar as you love and feel at one with those things which are difficult for you, to that extent will those circumstances be alleviated; if your mind is stayed upon the unity of the Creator, your own universe will become harmonious."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: circumstances alleviated and one's own universe harmonious, in proportion to the love."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditationOnUnity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaAlleviationByUnity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaClingingToThirdDensity a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No precise prediction of the Earth changes, and no time spent on preserving third-density existence"@en, "Keine genaue Vorhersage der Erdveränderungen, und keine Zeit für den Erhalt des Daseins in der dritten Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: it is neither permissible nor possible for us to tell you precisely what events will occur or when, because the vibration within the mind and heart of the peoples of the planet is determining and will determine the precise events; there is karma within the planet that must be adjusted as the cycle changes. The rain, wind and fire will destroy only things of the third density; spend no time concerning yourselves with maintaining your third-density existence after the vibration change to fourth density has been completed. If your graduation day has come, what is necessary for your emergence into fourth density will be done for you by helpers. You cling to the physical body as though your spirit were attached permanently to it; the spirit resides within a shell, and the spirit does not perish."@en ;
    skos:note "A refusal to predict given with its reason, which is also a caution against reading the passage as a prediction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaHarvest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 33-34; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHarvest a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The harvest at the end of a cycle"@en, "Die Ernte am Ende eines Zyklus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction calls the harvest a Judgment Day in which the one who judges is not a God apart but the God within; some go on to a new age of love and light in a positive density, others repeat the grade and relearn the lessons of love, and Hatonn calls the Confederation the Harvesters, attempting to increase by a relatively small percentage the number harvested into the path of love and understanding. Ra says that those who finish a cycle of experience are separated by their own choice into the vibratory distortion most comfortable to them, a process watched by nurturing beings; the spirit complex of each harvested entity moves along the line of light until the light grows too glaring, and there stops. A major cycle is approximately 25,000 years; those who have progressed may be harvested at the end of three, approximately 75,000 to 76,000 years, and all are harvested at that end regardless of progress, because the planet has moved through the useful part of the dimension. Ra says the planetary changes are very trivial and that it does not concern itself with the conditions which bring about harvest, and that an estimate of the percentage to be harvested is meaningless because the harvesting is not yet."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 34-35; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 72; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 99-101; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHarvestThreshold a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A vibratory rate above a certain minimal level before the harvest into the path of love"@en, "Eine Schwingungsrate über einem bestimmten Mindestmaß vor der Ernte in den Pfad der Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: the choice is measured by the vibratory rate of the individual; it is necessary, if an individual is to join those who make the choice of love and understanding, for his rate of vibration to be above a certain minimal level. Many are close to it but, through continuing erroneous thought, fluctuate around it or drift away; many are high enough to travel with no difficulty into the coming density. Those above the level have already made the grade; those far below it cannot be helped by the Confederation at this time."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a minimal level is named as threshold, but not quantified in this part; the failure is put on the individual's thought, and the outcome, repeating the grade, is not observable within the life."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaHarvest ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaVibratoryRate ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Those not above the level are not harvested into the path of love and understanding and will have to repeat this particular grade of lessons and relearn the lessons of love (Introduction, p. 35)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 34-35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVerbalChoice a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The verbal choice means nothing: the choice is measured by its demonstration"@en, "Die ausgesprochene Wahl bedeutet nichts: die Wahl wird an ihrer Darlegung gemessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: each person on Earth will shortly make a choice, with no middle area, between the path of love and light and the other. The choice will not be made by saying I choose the path of love and light or I do not choose it; the verbal choice will mean nothing. It will be measured by the individual's demonstration of his choice, which the Confederation interprets easily, as his vibratory rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a declared choice without its demonstration is named as void; the failure is put on the individual's conduct."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaHarvest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 34; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaWanderer a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wanderers: beings of other densities incarnate on Earth to serve"@en, "Wanderer: Wesen anderer Dichten, zum Dienst auf der Erde inkarniert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction describes Wanderers as usually service-oriented people who have difficulty fitting into the planetary vibrations of Earth and often feel they do not belong, yet are often possessed of gifts in the arts, in teaching or in sharing a cheerful vibration; it says Ra suggests about sixty-five million, who have left other densities in harmonious environments for a job most difficult and dangerous, and that the Ra material will be most easily recognized as useful by Wanderers. Ra calls the Eighteenth Dynasty pharaoh Ikhnaton a Wanderer, who received its communication and blended his distortions with Ra's, and speaks of those who have chosen service and removed their mind/body/spirit complexes from one dimension to another, bringing many skills and understandings in totally latent form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 35-36; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 76; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 89; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaWandererCaughtInIllusion a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A Wanderer who cannot pierce the forgetting may be caught in the third-density illusion"@en, "Ein Wanderer, der das Vergessen nicht durchdringt, kann in der Illusion der dritten Dichte gefangen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "If a Wanderer cannot at least begin to pierce the forgetting process during his or her lifetime on Earth and remember the love and the light the person was intended to share, the Wanderer can conceivably become caught in the third-density illusion, collecting what may loosely be termed karma, and be delayed in arriving again at the home planet until all that is unbalanced in third density in this lifetime has been balanced."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the failure to begin piercing the forgetting within the lifetime is named, with the lifetime as the deadline and delay as the outcome, not observable; the failure is put on the Wanderer."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaWanderer ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 36; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaPsychicSurgery a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychic surgery: opening the body with the bare hands"@en, "Psychische Chirurgie: den Körper mit bloßen Händen öffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Philippine practice as Rueckert saw it: the healer, a religious man who has often spent ten or twelve years of his life praying to become a healer, walking in solitude in the volcanic mountains of Luzon, enters carrying nothing but perhaps a Bible, with an assistant who interprets and cleans up. He scans the body with his palms down, as an X-ray machine would; at the chosen site he presses his left hand firmly against the skin, the skin seems to separate, and the right hand enters and manipulates within the body; when the left hand is removed the incision vanishes without a scar. The Mexican healer Pachita, whose gift came to her on the battlefield with Pancho Villa's army, used a dull knife with a five-inch blade. The authors believe the opening, closing and blood are materializations of the same type as those of ghosts and UFOs."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the incision vanishing without scar or trace, and a distinct change of emotional and mental attitude in every patient Rueckert spoke to once the healer's hands were upon them, which the healers call the presence of the Holy Spirit and which she says should be considered part of the phenomenon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 43-45; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPsychicHealing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing by psychic surgery, in which nothing happens to the physical body"@en, "Heilung durch psychische Chirurgie, bei der dem physischen Körper nichts geschieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction calls psychic surgery, like all faith healing, impossible to prove, and truly a psychic form of healing: no patient has ever been lost, because nothing actually happens to the patient's physical body. In Rueckert's case the healer, told she had arthritis, found by scanning three cysts on her right ovary and a dropping of both ovaries from years of active life, which she had told no one but which her gynecologist had diagnosed; he pulled at what seemed organs to reposition the ovaries and removed three small, long pieces of bloody material with a hard centre."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 43-44; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPsychicSurgeryYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Psychic surgery yields the removal of the cysts"@en, "Psychische Chirurgie bringt die Entfernung der Zysten hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "On returning to the United States Rueckert had her gynecologist examine the area; he confirmed that the three cysts were no longer palpable. They have remained gone, and the comfort of her menstrual cycle is correspondingly far better. She could get no orthodox doctor to test the possible result of the Mexican work on her kidneys, because the test itself could put damaged kidneys into failure."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a physician's finding that the cysts were no longer palpable, and lasting comfort."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaPsychicSurgery ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPsychicHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 46; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMagneticHealing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magnetic healing: massage with oil, prayer and a visualized protective light"@en, "Magnetische Heilung: Massage mit Öl, Gebet und ein vorgestelltes Schutzlicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the operation the healer and assistant worked baby oil over the skin, massaging in silence; the introduction calls this a very simplified and unostentatious form of magnetic healing in which prayers are offered and a protective light is visualized around the affected area so that healing will be aided."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMagneticHealingYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Magnetic healing aids the healing"@en, "Magnetische Heilung unterstützt die Heilung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The prayers and the protective light visualized around the affected area are offered so that healing will be aided."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMagneticHealing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPsychicHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSpecimenAnalysisCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Analysis of the products of psychic surgery comes to nothing; gather data instead of proving"@en, "Die Analyse der Erzeugnisse psychischer Chirurgie führt zu nichts; Daten sammeln statt beweisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The authors never preserved specimens of psychic surgery, because they hold the materials to be materializations, and say they know this does not fulfil the rigors of the scientific method but believe they would find out nothing by analysing such manifestations. Many who have researched psychic surgery by analysis of its products have found either inconclusive results or null results indicating that it is a fraud. Investigation at the fringe is rewarding to the researcher who is patient and whose approach is simply to gather data rather than to attempt to prove, step by step, hypotheses about what he is researching."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the null result of analysis is announced in advance and explained by the nature of the materials, the same structure as the dampening controls at pmc:RaRigorousControlsDampen; the failure is put on the method of examination."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaPsychicSurgery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 44-46; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaFrontalLobeCommunication a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Communication with advanced civilizations through the frontal lobes of the brain"@en, "Verbindung mit fortgeschrittenen Zivilisationen durch die Stirnlappen des Gehirns"@de ;
    skos:definition "In 1972 McCarty took a course in consciousness expansion called brain self-control with a mountain man in a log cabin in the Colorado Rockies, and there learned for the first time of the possibility of communication with advanced civilizations from outer space not through man-made means such as radios or electronic gadgetry but through the use of the frontal lobes of the human brain."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported as a possibility McCarty learned of; no procedure is given in the work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 46-47; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaChallengingInTheNameOfChrist a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Challenging a new contact in the name of Christ"@en, "Einen neuen Kontakt im Namen Christi herausfordern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert, as she does in all cases, challenged the new entity in the name of Christ, demanding that it leave if it did not come as a messenger of Christ-consciousness; it remained, so she opened herself to its channel."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the entity remained under the challenge, and the channel was opened to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTranceChanneling a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trance channelling: the instrument leaves the body and the contact speaks through it"@en, "Trance-Channeln: das Instrument verlässt den Körper und der Kontakt spricht durch es"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert had always channelled consciously. In 1980, asked by a friend's widower to contact the dead woman, she consciously offered herself for the contact, became unaware of the passing of time, and on waking the widower had what sounded like his wife's voice on tape speaking through her; it was her first experience of trance, and she does not know how it occurred. In the Ra sessions she departs her physical body and Ra uses it to make the words, and she has no idea afterwards of what occurred. Ra says it has good contact with her because of her recent experiences with trance and that she is to be able to communicate its thoughts in the future."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: Elkins said that had he heard her from the next room without seeing her he would have been certain it was the dead woman speaking. The same passage says the trance work was extremely draining to her and that she asked not to continue it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 48-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 73; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTranceMayNotCome a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument's fear that the trance will not come: she remains conscious and receives no contact"@en, "Die Furcht des Instruments, die Trance werde nicht kommen: sie bleibt bei Bewusstsein und empfängt keinen Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert says that when trance must be obtained for the contact her disquiet grows close to near panic: she does not know how the procedure works and is always afraid that in this session nothing will happen, that she will remain conscious and receive no contact. This has never happened. Since no one in the group knows how to aid her beyond a certain point in achieving trance, there is nothing to be done but to move ahead."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the observable sign of failure is named, remaining conscious with no contact, together with the report that it has not occurred; no cause is named, and it is put on the instrument."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaTranceChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 48-49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaFreeWillChannelingNonsense a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Free will channelling can utter complete nonsense"@en, "Channeln mit freiem Willen kann völligen Unsinn hervorbringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert: the person who decides to become a vocal channel has already taken the difficult step of being willing to speak the words of one who is not controlled by the self. In free will channelling it is possible to choose to stop; it is also possible to utter complete nonsense, because the channel never knows in advance what the next concept will be. She adds that this has never occurred in her experience, and that in a society that teaches one to measure one's words it seems an irresponsible act to blurt out what comes into the mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: nonsense is named as the observable failure of the method, with its cause, the channel's not knowing the next concept; the failure is put on the instrument's method."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 48-49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMediumNotSource a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The medium is not the source: a sharp differentiation between the words and the channel"@en, "Das Medium ist nicht die Quelle: eine scharfe Trennung zwischen den Worten und dem Kanal"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert: what concerns her perhaps more than anything else is that a reader will consider her to have some sort of wisdom that Ra has and she does not. If the work impresses the reader, she asks for a sharp differentiation between the words and the medium through which they come, as one would not expect the water pipe to be responsible for the quality of the water. The group prepares itself through meditation and daily life, but what comes through stands on its own and cannot be said to reflect the wisdom or spiritual advancement of any member."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning against a misreading of the work by its own instrument."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContactReceiving ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTwoSessionsDailyTooWearing a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Two sessions a day for days at a time was much too wearing on the instrument"@en, "Zwei Sitzungen täglich über Tage hinweg zehrten das Instrument viel zu sehr aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "McCarty: the group learned session by session, by trial and error, how to support the instrument mentally, physically and spiritually. At first it held two sessions per day for days at a time; it has since learned that this was much too wearing on her, and averages about one session every week to ten days, which allows the greater care in preparation that seems required as sessions accumulate."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a count, two sessions a day for days at a time, with an observable outcome, the instrument worn down; the failure is put on the group's schedule and the instrument's strength."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaTranceChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaQuestionerIntuition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The questioner's foundation and intuition"@en, "Grundlage und Intuition des Fragenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "McCarty says the great bulk of the questioning is done by Elkins, who has the years of experience in investigating the UFO contactee phenomenon necessary to develop the intellectual foundation required to fit the pieces together, and the intuitive sense vital in following Ra's unexpected answers with further questions developed on the spur of the moment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Ra contact: a narrow band contact through the instrument in trance"@en, "Der Ra-Kontakt: ein Schmalbandkontakt durch das Instrument in Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "The working in which Ra speaks through the instrument in trance in answer to the questioner's queries. Ra says it sends a narrow band vibration and had to wait until the instrument was precisely tuned; it calls the contact a narrow band contact, in which electrical and electromagnetic energies are to be kept constant when their presence is necessary and absent otherwise. McCarty says Ra speaks quite slowly and forms each syllable with precise enunciation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 70; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 52, quoting session 88 (May 29, 1982); read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 50-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaSessionPreparation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Preparing a Ra session: massage, meditation, ritual of protection and the Circle of One"@en, "Vorbereitung einer Ra-Sitzung: Massage, Meditation, Schutzritual und der Kreis des Einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "McCarty's account of the series of steps which will best aid the group in successfully completing a session. The decision is made the night before; on the day the group has a light breakfast; McCarty gives the instrument a half-hour back massage to loosen her muscles and joints, since she will lie absolutely motionless for an hour to an hour and forty-five minutes; the group meditates so that the harmony of its daily life is intensified and its desires are unified into the single desire to see contact with Ra; it performs a ritual of protection and cleansing of the room; the instrument lies prone, covered with a white blanket, her eyes with a white cloth, three tape recorder microphones below her chin; she mentally recites the Prayer of St. Francis while Elkins aligns the table with Bible, candle, incense and chalice of water in a straight line with her head, as Ra recommended; he lights candle and incense, and he and McCarty walk the Circle of One and repeat the words which begin each contact. During the session McCarty meditates and sends light to the instrument."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 50-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 67; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSessionPreparationYieldsContact a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The preparation of the session aids the contact"@en, "Die Vorbereitung der Sitzung unterstützt den Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The steps are taken because they will best aid the group in successfully completing the session; at some point after the Circle of One the instrument departs her physical body and Ra uses it to make the words which answer the questioner."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaSessionPreparation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 50-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Photographs, pp. 52-68 (quoting sessions 2, 69 and 88)
#

pmc:RaPhotographyCautions a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Photographing a working: only an actual working, never the instrument in trance"@en, "Eine Arbeitssitzung fotografieren: nur eine wirkliche Sitzung, nie das Instrument in Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra, quoted at the head of the photographs: if pictures are taken of a working, the image must be that which is, an actual working with no sham or substitution of any material. It is inadvisable to photograph the instrument or any portion of the working room while the instrument is in trance, because this is a narrow band contact and Ra wishes electrical and electromagnetic energies kept constant when necessary and absent otherwise. Once the instrument is aware of the picture-taking, before or after the working, she shall be required to respond continuously to speech, assuring that no trance is imminent. The photographs are to tell the truth, be dated and be clear. The caption to one photograph says the instrument is singing Amazing Grace, as Ra instructed she should be constantly speaking if her eyes are covered during picture-taking."@en ;
    skos:note "Session 88 lies outside Book I; the passage is printed in Book I and cited from there."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 52, quoting session 88 (May 29, 1982); read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 60; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHairInterference a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Slight interference with the contact from the instrument's hair"@en, "Leichte Störung des Kontakts durch das Haar des Instruments"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra, quoted under a photograph: at this particular working there is some slight interference with the contact due to the hair of the instrument; it suggests combing this antenna-like material into a more orderly configuration prior to the working."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: Ra names interference with the contact and its cause, the disordered hair; the failure is put on the instrument's physical preparation. Session 69 lies outside Book I."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 54, quoting session 69 (August 29, 1981); read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 1, January 15, 1981, pp. 70-74
#

pmc:RaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ra, a social memory complex and humble messenger of the Law of One"@en, "Ra, ein soziales Gedächtniskomplex und demütiger Bote des Gesetzes des Einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The speaker introduces itself as Ra: those who are of the Law of One, in whose vibration the polarities are harmonized, the complexities simplified, the paradoxes solved; old upon this planet, having served with varying success in transmitting the Law of One; not a part of time. The identity of the vibration Ra is its identity, and its connection with the Egyptian Ra is congruency: as a group, a social memory complex, it made contact with the Egyptians. It says it voyaged outward from Venus, where at the sixth dimension its beings were golden, tall and somewhat delicate. The Circle of One calls it an humble messenger of the Law of One. Elkins calls it a sixth-density social memory complex which landed about 11,000 years ago as a sort of missionary."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ra" ;
    pm:nameRole "a social memory complex of the sixth density, member of the Confederation, an humble messenger of the Law of One" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 70-71; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 79; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 98; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMindBodySpiritComplex a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind/body/spirit complex"@en, "Der Geist/Körper/Seele-Komplex"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra's term for the human being and for any entity of a density: the complex of mind, body and spirit, which dwells within a hierarchy of vehicles, is distorted in various chosen ways, enters and leaves incarnation, and in the instrument must re-enter after trance. The body is a creature of the mind's creation; the mind controls the body; the spirit complex is the least distorted part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 72-73; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 83; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 95; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 97; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInfiniteCreatorNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The one infinite Creator"@en, "Der eine unendliche Schöpfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra greets and leaves the group in the love and the light of the one infinite Creator, which it identifies with the one that all things are, love/light, light/love; Hatonn says all thought generated is generated by the Creator, who is all things and in all places, whose infinite parts all have free will."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the one infinite Creator" ;
    pm:nameRole "the one that all things are, of which every entity is a part" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 70; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTuningBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument precisely tuned before Ra speaks"@en, "Das Instrument genau abgestimmt, bevor Ra spricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: I have not spoken through this instrument before; we had to wait until she was precisely tuned, as we send a narrow band vibration. Asked about the planetary changes, Ra says it preferred to wait until the instrument had again reached a proper state of depth of singleness or one-pointedness before speaking. In session 6 it says it is having difficulty communicating with the instrument and must deepen her state."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an untuned instrument is named as a state in which Ra does not speak, or speaks with difficulty; the outcome, delay or difficulty, is observable, and the failure is put on the instrument."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaTunedState ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Ra does not speak through the instrument until she is precisely tuned and waits again for the proper depth of one-pointedness; when her state is not deep enough it has difficulty communicating (session 1, pp. 70 and 72; session 6, p. 99)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 70; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 72; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 99; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDirectContactFailure a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Teaching by direct contact: the message distorted and the teachers acclaimed"@en, "Lehre durch unmittelbaren Kontakt: die Botschaft entstellt und die Lehrer verherrlicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says it spoke to one who heard and understood and was in a position to decree the Law of One, but the priests and peoples quickly distorted the message, robbing it of compassion; when it no longer had appropriate channels it removed itself from the now hypocritical position it had allowed itself to be placed in. Eleven thousand years ago it held the naive belief that it could teach by direct contact without danger to free will; it aided two cultures with the healing of distortions through crystals and ratios of shapes, and found the technology reserved largely for those with the distortion of power, which was not intended by the Law of One, and left. Ikhnaton's beliefs were accepted by very few and his priests gave lip service only. Its visit in its golden sixth-density form was relatively short, because it found itself acclaimed as other than its other-selves."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the failure of direct teaching is named three times with its observable outcome, distortion of the message, reservation of the technology for power, and acclamation; the failure is put on the hearers and on the method."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 71; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 76-77; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 98; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLawOfOne a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: that which is infinite cannot be many; in an infinite Creator there is only unity. In truth there is no right or wrong, no polarity, for all will be reconciled; you are every thing, every being, every emotion, every event; you are unity, you are infinity, you are love/light, light/love; this is the Law of One. Restated: all things are one; there is no polarity, no right or wrong, no disharmony, but only identity; all is one, and that one is love/light, light/love, the infinite Creator. There are behaviours and thought-forms consonant with its understanding and practice. It is available to any social memory complex that has decided to strive together for any purpose, service to others or service to self, and all entities learn, some rapidly, some slowly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 71-72; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 100; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 108; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDistortion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Distortion: the chosen departure from the understanding of unity"@en, "Verzerrung: die gewählte Abweichung vom Verständnis der Einheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says the mind/body/spirit complex amuses itself by distorting the unity in various ways; this distortion is not in any case necessary but is chosen by each as an alternative to understanding the complete unity of thought which binds all things. Ra calls free will, the Law of Confusion, one of the more significant primal distortions of the Law of One, healing another, and teach/learning the Law of One in one of its most elementary distortions; it describes itself as desiring to decrease distortions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 71-72; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 75; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 84; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 52, quoting session 88 (May 29, 1982); read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaTeachLearning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Learn/teaching: teaching what one learns, sharing one's light"@en, "Lernen/Lehren: lehren, was man lernt, sein Licht teilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the distinction between yourself and others is not visible to us, so to learn is the same as to teach. Each in the group is striving to use, digest and diversify the information without distortion; the few whom you will illuminate by sharing your light are far more than enough reason for the greatest possible effort; to serve one is to serve all; to learn/teach or teach/learn is the only activity worth doing. To share Ra's communications with others, if that is the group's desire, is what Ra calls teach/learning, the Law of One in one of its most elementary distortions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 72-73; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 75; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaNotTeachingWhatYouLearn a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Teaching what one does not learn does little good"@en, "Lehren, was man nicht lernt, nützt wenig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: to learn is the same as to teach unless you are not teaching what you are learning, in which case you have done you/them little good; this understanding should be pondered."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the gap between what is taught and what is learned is named as what makes the effort useless; the failure is put on the teacher, and the outcome is not observable."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaTeachLearning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 72; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRegularizedVibration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Regularizing and crystallizing one's own patterns of vibration"@en, "Die eigenen Schwingungsmuster regulieren und kristallisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says that sharing its communications with others would, in its perception, be most helpful in regularizing and crystallizing the group's own patterns of vibration upon the levels of experience called life; if one is illuminated, are not all illuminated?"@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 75; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTeachLearningYieldsRegularizedVibration a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sharing the communications yields the regularizing of one's own vibration"@en, "Das Teilen der Mitteilungen bringt die Regulierung der eigenen Schwingung hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: if it be your desire to share our communications with others, we have the distortion towards a perception that this would be most helpful in regularizing and crystallizing your own patterns of vibration."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaTeachLearning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaRegularizedVibration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 75; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRecentTranceBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument's recent experiences with trance before the good contact"@en, "Die jüngsten Tranceerfahrungen des Instruments vor dem guten Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: we have good contact with this instrument because of her recent experiences with trance; she is to be able to communicate our thoughts in your future. The introduction places her first two trances, for a dead friend, a few days before the Ra contact began."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order in the weak sense: Ra gives the prior trance as the reason for the good contact and not as an instruction, and says nothing of a contact without it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaTranceChanneling ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 73; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaInstrumentRecall a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Bringing the instrument back: silence, her name until she answers, hands at the neck, charged water"@en, "Das Instrument zurückholen: Stille, ihr Name bis zur Antwort, Hände am Nacken, geladenes Wasser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra advises care in disturbing the channel and gives the proper procedure for aiding an instrument who needs to re-enter her mind/body/spirit complex: first a brief period of silence; then the repetition of her name, the vibration of the nickname which contains the most love, until an answer is obtained; then the laying on of hands at the neck region for a brief period, so that she may recharge batteries not full of the essence of this field; and finally a gift of water into which the love of all present has been given. If the sessions are held when the sun does not light the room, it is best to call the instrument before the light is turned on. McCarty reports the procedure as the group performs it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 73-74; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 80; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, p. 62; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentRestoration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration of the instrument after trance: recharging and comfort"@en, "Wiederherstellung des Instruments nach der Trance: Aufladen und Trost"@de ;
    skos:definition "The restoration of the instrument as she re-enters her body: the recharging of batteries depleted of the essence of this field, and the comfort of the charged water, owing to her distortions' great sensitivity towards the vibrations of love. Ra says it spent time explaining how the distortions of fatigue may be ameliorated because the instrument is quite fatigued but her heart is such that she remains open and useful as a channel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 73-74; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentRecallYieldsRestoration a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The procedure of recall restores the instrument"@en, "Das Verfahren des Zurückholens stellt das Instrument wieder her"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the laying on of hands lets the instrument recharge batteries; the gift of water into which the love of all present has been given will restore this entity, and the charged water will effect comfort."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaInstrumentRecall ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaInstrumentRestoration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 73-74; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaChargedWater a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Charging the water: hands over the chalice, visualizing love entering it"@en, "Das Wasser laden: die Hände über dem Kelch, die eintretende Liebe vorgestellt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the charging of the water is done by those present placing their hands over the glass and visualizing the power of love entering the water, which charges that very effective medium with those vibrations. Asked which vessel, Ra says that only the chalice behind the instrument's head should be used, since the virgin material living in the chalice accepts, retains and responds to the love vibration activated by their being-ness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 74; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), pp. 85-86; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaChargedWaterYieldsRestoration a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The charged water comforts the instrument"@en, "Das geladene Wasser tröstet das Instrument"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: her distortions contain great sensitivity towards the vibrations of love, and the charged water will effect comfort; that and only that chalice shall be the most beneficial."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaChargedWater ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaInstrumentRestoration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), pp. 73-74; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 86; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTouchBeforeResponse a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument is not to be touched until she has responded to her name"@en, "Das Instrument ist nicht zu berühren, bevor sie auf ihren Namen geantwortet hat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: under no circumstances should this instrument be touched until she has responded to her name."@en ;
    skos:note "No reason or consequence is given in the passage."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaInstrumentRecall ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 74; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentEnergyLow a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument's physical energy grows low and Ra must leave"@en, "Die körperliche Energie des Instruments wird gering und Ra muss gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: I do not wish to take this instrument beyond her capacity for physical energy; it grows low; therefore I must leave this instrument. In session 2 it says the instrument begins to lose energy and asks for one more query; in session 3 it advises a fairly rapid ending; in session 4 it says the instrument is nurtured by approximately this length of work. In session 2 the questioner states that when the instrument becomes fatigued the group wants to cut off communication and continue when she is recharged."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the instrument's physical energy is named as the limit, and the observable outcome is that Ra ends the session; the failure is put on the instrument."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 74; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 77; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 78; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 2, January 20, 1981, pp. 75-80
#

pmc:RaQueryFormat a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ra answers queries and does not choose the questions"@en, "Ra beantwortet Fragen und wählt die Fragen nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says its social memory complex has one particular method of communicating with those few who may harmonize their distortions with its own, to respond to queries for information, and that it does not consider it has the right/duty to share its perceptions on any subject but philosophy without direct question. It will not suggest the proper series of questions, which is the questioner's prerogative as free agent of the Law of One, because it cannot discern the distortions of the societal mind of this people; it cannot tell the questioner what to ask. It weights its answers by its perception of their importance and offers them unless a question contains the potential for an answer that may infringe upon free will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 75; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 78-79; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 82; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 89; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 103; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHistoricalInterestCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A spurious interest: no stress on Ra's history, whose teaching is philosophical"@en, "Ein falsches Interesse: kein Gewicht auf Ras Geschichte, deren Lehre philosophisch ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra waited for a second query before answering about its history so as to emphasize that a span of several thousand years creates a spurious type of interest; it asks that the proper lack of stress be placed upon its experiences in local space/time, since its teach/learning is philosophical rather than historical, and calls the request harmless if properly evaluated. It iterates the unimportance of the capstone data, and calls the question of present-day craft unimportant, the Law of One being what it is here to express."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning of the work against a misreading of its own narrative."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContactReceiving ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 75-76; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 82; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 102; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaCrystalHealing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Crystal healing through a purified channel and a ratio of shapes"@en, "Kristallheilung durch einen gereinigten Kanal und ein Verhältnis von Formen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the principle of crystal healing rests on the hierarchical structure of the illusion that is the body. Some crystals work upon the energies coming into the spiritual body, some upon the distortions from spirit to mind, some balance the distortions between mind and body; all are charged through purified channels. The other ingredient is proper alignment with the energy fields of the planet and the cosmic streamings entering its aura, so that an appropriate ratio of shapes and placement within them aids the untangling or balancing. The choice of crystal is very critical; yet a crystalline structure such as a diamond or ruby can be used by a purified channel filled with the love/light of One in almost any application. This takes initiation, and few have persevered through the distortion leavings it causes. Ra says the pyramids came from this healing work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 76-78; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHealing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing: the realization of the Law of One, the healer only its catalyst"@en, "Heilung: die Verwirklichung des Gesetzes des Einen, der Heiler nur ihr Katalysator"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: one of the primal distortions of the Law of One is healing. Healing occurs when a mind/body/spirit complex realizes, deep within itself, the Law of One, that there is no disharmony, no imperfection, that all is complete and whole and perfect; the intelligent infinity within that complex then re-forms the illusion of body, mind or spirit to a form congruent with the Law of One. The healer acts as energizer or catalyst for this completely individual process; the working exists in and of itself, and the healer, like the instrument for Ra's words, can take no thought for it by example or exercise. The healing/working is a form of channelling some distortion of intelligent infinity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 94; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaCrystalHealingYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Crystal healing yields the balancing of mind/body/spirit distortions"@en, "Kristallheilung bringt den Ausgleich der Verzerrungen von Geist, Körper und Seele hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says it aided two cultures in technical ways having to do with the healing of mind/body/spirit complex distortions through the crystal appropriate to the distortion, placed within an appropriate series of ratios of time/space material; the crystals work upon the spiritual body, the passage from spirit to mind and the balance of mind and body."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaCrystalHealing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 76-77; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPurifiedChannel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The purified channel, filled with the love/light of One"@en, "Der gereinigte Kanal, erfüllt vom Liebe/Licht des Einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The purified or initiated channel for the Law of One: the healer whose relative crystallization charges the crystal, the purified and dedicated channel or energizer for the love/light of the infinite Creator to flow through, prepared by the initiatory method in mind, body and spirit for service in the Creator's work. Ra says only an individual purified of all flaws could move a mountain alone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 77-78; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), pp. 84-85; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaCrystallizationOfHealer a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The healer's crystallization before the crystal is charged"@en, "Die Kristallisation des Heilers, bevor der Kristall geladen wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: all of these crystal healings are charged through purified channels; without the relative crystallization of the healer working with the crystal, the crystal will not be properly charged. Using a diamond or ruby in almost any application takes initiation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a healer without crystallization is named as the reason the crystal is not charged; the outcome is not observable as such, and the failure is put on the healer."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:RaCrystalHealing ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaPurifiedChannel ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without the relative crystallization of the healer working with the crystal, the crystal will not be properly charged (session 2, p. 77)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 77-78; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentMisuse a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument not correctly used, and so fatigued without need"@en, "Das Instrument nicht richtig gebraucht und daher unnötig ermüdet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra, asked about the proper use of the instrument: this mind/body/spirit is not being correctly used and therefore is experiencing unnecessary distortions of body in the area of fatigue. It then gives the Circle of One, the alignment and the artifacts, and says these elaborations on the technique of trance will ease the minds of those about the instrument as they perceive improvement in her fatigue."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: incorrect use is named as the cause of observable fatigue; the failure is put on the group's procedure."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaTranceChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 78-80; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaCircleOfOne a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Circle of One: walking the circle and speaking the dialogue of the Law"@en, "Der Kreis des Einen: den Kreis abschreiten und die Wechselrede des Gesetzes sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the vibrations may well be purified by a simple turning to the circle of One and the verbal vibration while doing so of the following dialogue. Question: What is the Law? Answer: The Law is One. Question: Why are we here? Answer: We seek the Law of One. Question: Why do we seek Ra? Answer: Ra is an humble messenger of the Law of One. Both together: Rejoice then and purify this place in the Law of One; let no thought-form enter the circle we have walked about this instrument, for the Law is One. The instrument should at this time be in trance. McCarty reports that he and Elkins walk the Circle of One and repeat the words which begin each contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 79; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPurifiedPlace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The purified place: no thought-form within the walked circle"@en, "Der gereinigte Ort: keine Gedankenform im abgeschrittenen Kreis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state of the working place after the Circle of One: its vibrations purified in the Law of One, and no thought-form to enter the circle walked about the instrument."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 79; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaCircleOfOneYieldsPurifiedPlace a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Circle of One purifies the vibrations of the place"@en, "Der Kreis des Einen reinigt die Schwingungen des Ortes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the vibrations may well be purified by a simple turning to the circle of One and the speaking of the dialogue."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaCircleOfOne ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPurifiedPlace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 79; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaArtifactArrangement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Arranging the instrument and the artifacts: chalice, Bible, incense, candle, twenty degrees north-by-northeast"@en, "Anordnung des Instruments und der Gegenstände: Kelch, Bibel, Weihrauch, Kerze, zwanzig Grad Nordnordost"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the proper alignment is with the head pointed twenty degrees north-by-northeast, the direction from which the less distorted New Age distortions of love/light emanate. Because the instrument is sensitive through all her senses: place at her head a virgin chalice of water; to the centre the book most closely aligned with her mental distortions allied with the Law of One, the Bible she touches most frequently, opened to the Gospel of John, chapter one; to the other side a small amount of incense in a virgin censer; to the rear of the book a white candle. She is strengthened by a white robe, and is to be covered and prone, the eyes covered. Corrections in later sessions: the artifacts to be placed at her head; the incense perpendicular to the plane of twenty degrees north-by-northeast, checked by eye; more support to the neck; the candle rotated clockwise about ten degrees each session; the objects centred with geometric care, checked from time to time, and not exposed to space/time in which work is not of importance; the spine straighter; the placement and orientation of the symbols continually monitored."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 79-80; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 81; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 96; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), pp. 111-112; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Photographs, pp. 53-57; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentBalance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument balanced, energized from the lower to the higher, and not fatigued"@en, "Das Instrument ausgeglichen, vom Niederen zum Höheren belebt, und nicht ermüdet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra explains the arrangement as a distortion balancer: the incense acts as energizer to the physical body of the instrument, signifying its humanity, and must be perceived from the same relative angle as the opened Bible balanced by the lighted candle, signifying love/light and light/love, which give her mental and emotional distortion complex the sight of paradise and peace which it seeks. Thus energized from the lower to the higher, the instrument becomes balanced and does not grow fatigued."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: Ra reports the instrument much aided by these precautions (session 3, p. 85), balanced due to the group's care (session 6, p. 103), usable with minimal distortion and without depleting her to any significant extent (session 7, p. 109) and well balanced (session 8, p. 112); and says those about her will perceive improvement in her fatigue (session 2, pp. 79-80)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 81; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaArtifactArrangementYieldsBalance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The arrangement of the artifacts yields the instrument's balance and ease of fatigue"@en, "Die Anordnung der Gegenstände bringt das Gleichgewicht des Instruments und die Linderung der Ermüdung hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: these elaborations on the technique of trance will ease the minds of those about the instrument as they perceive improvement in her fatigue; with the incense correctly angled to the Bible and candle, the instrument becomes balanced and does not grow fatigued, which will enable the teach/learning to proceed more easily."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaArtifactArrangement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaInstrumentBalance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), pp. 79-80; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 81; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 3, January 21, 1981, pp. 81-86
#

pmc:RaNonServingParticipants a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Those not wishing to serve others above all else are to take no part in a session"@en, "Wer nicht vor allem anderen dienen will, soll an keiner Sitzung teilhaben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says the beginning account of purpose was acceptable because those speaking desire to serve; otherwise the attendant emphasis in mind complexities would not have been affected properly. It cautions the group to guard against those who are not wishing to serve others above all else from taking part in the beginning or lending their distortions to any session, as Ra would then be unable properly to blend its distortions with those of the instrument."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the presence of a participant not wishing to serve others is named as what makes the blending with the instrument impossible; the failure is put on the group's harmony."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 81; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaSpeakingToTheIntelligenceOfRock a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking to the intelligence of the rock and making a request"@en, "Zur Intelligenz des Gesteins sprechen und eine Bitte stellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the energy within all that is created is intelligent and hierarchical; as the mind/body/spirit complex dwells within a hierarchy of vehicles, so does each atom of a material such as rock. When one can speak to that intelligence, the finite energy of the physical rock/body is put into contact with the infinite power resident in the more well-tuned bodies, human or rock. With this connection made, a request may be given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 83; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMovingStone a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Splitting and moving stone, and moving mountains, by the intelligence of infinity"@en, "Gestein spalten und bewegen, und Berge versetzen, durch die Intelligenz der Unendlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the intelligence of infinite rock-ness communicates to its physical vehicle, and the splitting and moving desired is carried out through the displacement of the energy field of rock-ness from finity to infinity, by the cooperation of the infinite understanding of the Creator indwelling in the living rock; this is the mechanism of many things not subject to present analysis of action at a distance. Faith and intelligent infinity are congruent, one a spiritual term, the other acceptable to those who seek with measure and pen. Ra says it built the larger pyramids by its ability, using the forces of One, the Great Pyramid as thought-form of everlasting rock, others with stone moved from one place to another."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 78; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), pp. 83-84; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSpeakingToRockYieldsMovingStone a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking to the intelligence of the rock yields its splitting and moving"@en, "Das Sprechen zur Intelligenz des Gesteins bringt sein Spalten und Bewegen hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: with this connection made, a request may be given; the intelligence of infinite rock-ness communicates to its physical vehicle, and that splitting and moving which is desired is then carried out; in this way that which is required is accomplished."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaSpeakingToTheIntelligenceOfRock ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaMovingStone ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 83; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMountainMovingPurity a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Purity of all flaws before one individual moves a mountain; a mass mind may with distortion"@en, "Reinheit von allen Fehlern, bevor ein Einzelner einen Berg versetzt; ein Massengeist vermag es mit Verzerrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra corrects the questioner: there is a distinction between individual power through the Law of One and the combined, societal memory complex understanding of it. In the first case only the one individual, purified of all flaws, could move a mountain; in the case of mass understanding of unity, each individual may contain an acceptable amount of distortion and yet the mass mind could move mountains."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order: a condition stated as a necessity without a consequence of its absence."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaMovingStone ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaPurifiedChannel ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 84; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaProgressionOfLaws a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "From the laws of love to the laws of light, the Law of One and the Law of Foreverness"@en, "Von den Gesetzen der Liebe zu den Gesetzen des Lichts, dem Gesetz des Einen und dem Gesetz der Immerwährung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the progress is normally from the understanding the questioner now seeks to a dimension of understanding governed by the laws of love and seeking the laws of light; those who vibrate with the Law of Light seek the Law of One; those who vibrate with the Law of One seek the Law of Foreverness. Ra cannot say what lies beyond this dissolution of the unified self with all that there is, for it still seeks to become all that there is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 84; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaWorshipCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The pyramid made to appear built, not thought, lest its builders be worshipped"@en, "Die Pyramide so gemacht, dass sie gebaut und nicht gedacht erscheint, damit ihre Erbauer nicht verehrt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: under the Law of Confusion it wished to make a healing machine as efficacious as possible but did not desire the mystery to be penetrated in such a way that it became worshipped as builder of a miraculous pyramid; thus it appears to be made, not thought."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaMovingStone ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), pp. 84-85; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaPyramidInitiation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation in the pyramid: sensory deprivation below, the focused point above"@en, "Einweihung in der Pyramide: Reizentzug unten, der gebündelte Punkt oben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the pyramids were built first to have a properly oriented place of initiation for those who wished to become purified or initiated channels for the Law of One. The first use of the shape concerns the body: the going down into the pyramid for deprivation of sensory input so that the body may, in a sense, be dead and another life begin. The initiation of spirit was more carefully designed as to time/space ratios: if the side is divided into four equal triangles, the intersection at the first level on each of the four sides forms a horizontal diamond, whose middle is the place where the energies streaming from the infinite dimensions intersect the mind/body/spirit complexes; the initiate was placed on the centre line at that height. The pyramid needed to be large enough to create the impression of towering size, so that the entrance point of intelligent infinity would completely pervade and fill the channel, the entire body resting in the focused area."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 78; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 87-88; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaIntelligentInfinityGateway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The gateway to intelligent infinity"@en, "Das Tor zur intelligenten Unendlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: in the pyramid the one to be initiated would by mind be able to perceive and then channel the gateway to intelligent infinity. Paranormal abilities are effected by the opening of a pathway or shuttle into intelligent infinity; some have a random hole or gateway in their spirit energy field. Those not oriented toward service to others nevertheless find and can use the gateway, at all densities of this octave, and systems of study enable the seeker of separation to gain these gateways."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 87; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 97-98; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 108-109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPyramidInitiationYieldsGateway a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation at the focused point yields the perceiving and channelling of the gateway"@en, "Einweihung am gebündelten Punkt bringt das Wahrnehmen und Leiten des Tores hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: it was designed that the one to be initiated would, by mind, be able to perceive and then channel this gateway to intelligent infinity; this was the second point of designing this specific shape."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaPyramidInitiation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaIntelligentInfinityGateway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 87; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPurifiedChannelForHealing a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The initiatory method before the healing in the pyramid"@en, "Die Einweihung vor der Heilung in der Pyramide"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the healing machine and the device for initiation are part of one complex of love/light intent. To use the healing properly it was important to have a purified and dedicated channel, or energizer, for the love/light of the infinite Creator to flow through; thus the initiatory method was necessary to prepare the mind, the body and the spirit for service in the Creator's work. The two are integral."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order: called necessary, without a stated consequence."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:RaPyramidHealing ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:RaPyramidInitiation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 85; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMindBeforeBody a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind known and initiated before the body"@en, "Der Geist erkannt und eingeweiht vor dem Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: before the body can be initiated, the mind must be initiated; this is the point from which most adepts of the present cycle find their mind/body/spirit complexes distorted. When the character and personality that is the true identity of the mind has been discovered, the body then must be known in each and every way. In the training of the healer, firstly the mind must be known to itself; the second part has to do with the disciplines of the body; and the mental disciplines are given before the study of the body complexes."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order. The remark about most adepts of the present cycle is as near as the sessions come to a consequence, but it does not say what follows from initiating the body first."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:RaBodyDisciplines ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:RaMentalDisciplines ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 91; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), pp. 94-95; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 4, January 22, 1981, pp. 87-93
#

pmp:RaPyramidHealing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing in the pyramid: channel and patient resting in the focused point"@en, "Heilung in der Pyramide: Kanal und Kranker ruhen im gebündelten Punkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: it was necessary for healing purposes that both channel and the one to be healed be able to rest within the focused point of the pyramid. Each size of pyramid has its own point of streaming in of intelligent infinity, so that a tiny pyramid placed below or above a body has specific and various effects depending on the placement of the body relative to that entrance point. Pyramid after pyramid, charged by the crystal and initiate, was designed to balance the incoming energy of the One Creation with the distortions of the planetary mind/body/spirit. A pyramid can be built today from any material, only the ratios of time/space complexes being critical."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 78; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 88; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPyramidHealingYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Healing in the pyramid yields the healing of people and planet"@en, "Heilung in der Pyramide bringt die Heilung von Menschen und Planet hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the second purpose of the pyramids was to guide the initiates in developing a healing of the people whom they sought to aid, and of the planet itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaPyramidHealing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 2 (January 20, 1981), p. 78; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 88; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaGizaOutOfTune a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Pyramid like a piano out of tune"@en, "Die Große Pyramide wie ein verstimmtes Klavier"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the large pyramid at Giza, like many other pyramid structures, is like the piano out of tune; it plays the tune, but so poorly; the disharmony jangles the sensitivity. Only the ghost of the streaming remains, because the streaming points have shifted with the shifting electromagnetic field of the planet, and because of the discordant vibratory complexes of those who have used the initiatory and healing place for less compassionate purposes. Ra adds that the time of the pyramids is past."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: two causes are named, the shifted streaming points and the discordant use, for a structure that no longer serves; the outcome is not observable in the terms given, and the failure is put on the planet's field and on former users."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaPyramidHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 88-89; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInnerDisciplineForPyramidUse a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The inner disciplines of the channels before a pyramid serves initiation or healing"@en, "Die inneren Disziplinen der Kanäle, bevor eine Pyramide der Einweihung oder Heilung dient"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: it is quite possible to build a pyramid structure, the material not being critical, merely the ratios of time/space complexes; however, the use of the structure for initiation and healing depends completely upon the inner disciplines of the channels attempting such work."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order: the dependence is total but its consequence is not spelled out."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:RaPyramidHealing ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:RaHealerTraining ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 88; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHealingWithoutStructures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing without structures, for those whose purity is one with intelligent infinity"@en, "Heilung ohne Bauwerke, für jene, deren Reinheit eins ist mit der intelligenten Unendlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the streamings from the universe, when Ra came, required a certain understanding of purity; as they revolved this changed to a more enlightened view of purity, so that there are those among the people at this time whose purity is already one with intelligent infinity. Without the use of structures, healer/patient can gain healing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 89; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaNativeHealingAbility a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The healing ability brought into this incarnation, and the two kinds of healers"@en, "Die in diese Inkarnation mitgebrachte Heilfähigkeit, und die zwei Arten von Heilern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra agrees that the first step is to find an individual with ability brought with him into this incarnation, and that it can instruct such a one. Two kinds there are who can heal: those such as the questioner who, having the innate distortion toward knowledge-giving of the Law of One, can heal but do not; and those who, showing no significant distortion toward the Law of One in mind, body or spirit, nevertheless have opened a channel to the same ability and heal without proper training. Many systems of teaching healing are proper for the various kinds of mind/body/spirit complexes, each type pursuing its own learning. Asked whether it will train the group in healing, Ra says it will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 89-90; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLifeNotEqualWork a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A healer whose life does not equal his work may have to cease healing"@en, "Ein Heiler, dessen Leben seinem Werk nicht entspricht, muss das Heilen vielleicht aufgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: those whose life does not equal their work may find some difficulty in absorbing the energy of intelligent infinity, and thus become quite distorted in such a way as to cause disharmony in themselves and others, and perhaps even find it necessary to cease the healing activity. Those who seek to serve and are willing to be trained in thought, word and action are those who will be able to comfortably maintain the distortion toward service in healing."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the gap between life and work is named as cause, with observable outcomes, disharmony in self and others and the end of healing; the failure is put on the healer."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaNativeHealingAbility ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 90; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaHealerTraining a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The training of the healer in three areas: mind, body, spirit"@en, "Die Ausbildung des Heilers in drei Bereichen: Geist, Körper, Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra's synopsis of the program: firstly, the mind must be known to itself, the most demanding part of healing work, and if the mind knows itself the most important aspect of healing has occurred; secondly, the disciplines of the body complexes, which in the present streamings concern the balance between love and wisdom in the use of the body in its natural functions, from its dense aspects to the finest energy pathways, all natural functions capable of being transmuted to the sacramental; thirdly, the spiritual, in which the first two are connected through the attainment of contact with intelligent infinity, the spirit integrating the upreaching yearning of the mind/body energy with the downpouring of infinite intelligence, as the two poles of a magnet. There should be fairly specific exercises of mind, body and spirit; Ra, not incarnate, can guide and specify but cannot show by example, which it calls a handicap."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 90-92; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHealerTrainingYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Training in thought, word and action yields a healer who can maintain the service"@en, "Ausbildung in Gedanke, Wort und Tat bringt einen Heiler hervor, der den Dienst halten kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: those of the first type, who seek to serve and are willing to be trained in thought, word and action, are those who will be able to comfortably maintain the distortion toward service in the area of healing."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaHealerTraining ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 90; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMindKnownToItself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind known to itself, the most important aspect of healing"@en, "Der sich selbst erkennende Geist, der wichtigste Teil der Heilung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: if the mind knows itself, then the most important aspect of healing has occurred; consciousness is the microcosm of the Law of One. In the initiation, the character and personality that is the true identity of the mind is to be discovered before the body is known."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 91; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHealingNotNecessary a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "To understand the Law of One it is not necessary to heal or to show any manifestation"@en, "Um das Gesetz des Einen zu verstehen, ist es nicht nötig zu heilen oder etwas zu zeigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: it is to be once more iterated that healing is but one distortion of the Law of One; to reach an undistorted understanding of that law it is not necessary to heal or to show any manifestation, but only to exercise the discipline of understanding."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning against taking the healing program for the goal of the teaching."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaHealerTraining ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHealerResponsibility a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A healer who asks to learn takes responsibility for the asking"@en, "Ein Heiler, der zu lernen bittet, übernimmt Verantwortung für die Bitte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: a healer asking to learn must take the distortion understood as responsibility for that ask/receiving; this is an honor/duty which must be carefully considered in free will before the asking. In session 5 the questioner says the group has decided to accept, if offered, the honor/duty of learning the healing process."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaHealerTraining ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 92; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 94; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTwoSessionsPerDay a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The instrument capable of two sessions a day"@en, "Das Instrument zu zwei Sitzungen am Tag fähig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: this instrument is capable of two sessions a day, the activity being equivalent to a strenuous working day on the physical level."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 92-93; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaInstrumentNourishment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeding the instrument beyond her normal intake and guarding her from overactivity"@en, "Das Instrument über ihr gewohntes Maß hinaus ernähren und vor Überanstrengung bewahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the instrument must be encouraged to keep her bodily complex strong by the ingestion of foodstuffs to an extent exceeding her normal intake, because of the physical material Ra uses to speak; and her activities must be monitored to prevent overactivity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 92-93; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaNourishmentBeforeTwoSessions a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "More food and less activity before two sessions a day"@en, "Mehr Nahrung und weniger Tätigkeit vor zwei Sitzungen am Tag"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: if these admonishments are considered, the two sessions would be possible; we do not wish to deplete this instrument."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a threshold, food beyond the normal intake and activity held below a strenuous day, with depletion of the instrument as the outcome; the failure is put on the instrument's care. McCarty's report that two sessions a day proved much too wearing (pmc:RaTwoSessionsDailyTooWearing) stands against the capacity here; see pmc:RaTwoSessionsDispute."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaTwoSessionsPerDay ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:RaInstrumentNourishment ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The instrument would be depleted: only if these admonishments are considered would the two sessions be possible (session 4, pp. 92-93)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 92-93; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTwoSessionsDispute a pm:Disputing ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the instrument can bear two sessions a day: Ra and the group's experience"@en, "Ob das Instrument zwei Sitzungen am Tag tragen kann: Ra und die Erfahrung der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra says in session 4 that the instrument is capable of two sessions a day if she eats beyond her normal intake and her activities are monitored to prevent overactivity. McCarty writes in the introduction, two years later, that the group held two sessions per day for days at a time when the contact began and has since learned that this was much too wearing on her, and now holds about one session every week to ten days."@en ;
    skos:note "Both sides stand in the same book. Ra's statement is conditional and McCarty does not say whether the conditions were kept, so the report does not refute it; it is the one place in this part where the instrument's account and the contact's account of her capacity can be laid side by side."@en ;
    pm:disputedClaim "Whether the instrument can sustain two sessions a day under the stated conditions" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), pp. 92-93; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 5, January 23, 1981, pp. 94-96
#

pmc:RaSilenceOfSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Silence of self at a steady state: the key that opens the mind like a door"@en, "Stille des Selbst in stetem Zustand: der Schlüssel, der den Geist wie eine Tür öffnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the prerequisite of mental work is the ability to retain silence of self at a steady state when required by the self. The mind must be opened like a door; the key is silence. Within the door lies a hierarchical construction which may be likened to geography and in some ways geometry, for the hierarchy is quite regular, bearing inner relationships."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 94; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSilenceBeforeMentalWork a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Silence of self before the disciplines of the mind"@en, "Stille des Selbst vor den Disziplinen des Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra begins the mental learn/teaching necessary for contact with intelligent infinity by naming its prerequisite: the ability to retain silence of self at a steady state when required by the self."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order: the text calls it the prerequisite and gives no consequence."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:RaMentalDisciplines ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaSilenceOfSelf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 94; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMentalDisciplines a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The five disciplines of the mind: balancing each thought with its antithesis, in self and in others"@en, "Die fünf Disziplinen des Geistes: jeden Gedanken mit seinem Gegenteil ausgleichen, in sich und in anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: to begin to master the mental disciplines it is necessary to examine the self and internalize the polarity of this dimension. First: where one finds patience one must consciously find the corresponding impatience and vice versa, since each thought has its antithesis; identify what one approves and disapproves of in oneself and balance each positive and negative charge with its equal, discovering the completeness the mind contains. Second: accept this completeness, not picking and choosing among attributes, which builds the roles that cause blockages; each acceptance smooths part of the distortions judgment engenders. Third: repeat the first with the gaze outward toward the entities one meets, mirroring in one's understanding patience/impatience when viewing patience and impatience/patience when viewing impatience, as subtle work. Fourth: accept the other-self polarities, mirroring the second. Fifth: observe the geographical and geometrical relationships and ratios of the mind, the other mind, the mass mind and the infinite mind."@en ;
    skos:note "The steps are numbered by the text and given in order; the fifth is named without exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), pp. 94-95; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMentalDisciplinesYieldMindKnown a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The disciplines of the mind yield the mind known to itself and its judgment smoothed"@en, "Die Disziplinen des Geistes bringen den sich selbst erkennenden Geist und die geglättete Urteilskraft hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the disciplines of the mind involve examining the self and discovering the completeness of the mind within oneself; each acceptance smooths part of the many distortions that the faculty called judgment engenders."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMentalDisciplines ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaMindKnownToItself ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), pp. 94-95; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaContactWithIntelligentInfinity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with intelligent infinity"@en, "Kontakt mit intelligenter Unendlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: in the spiritual area of the healer's training the disciplines of mind and body are connected through the attainment of contact with intelligent infinity, and the first of the three teachings is the mental learn/teaching necessary for that contact. Faith and intelligent infinity are congruent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 83; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 4 (January 22, 1981), p. 91; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 94; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMentalDisciplinesBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The mental learn/teaching before contact with intelligent infinity"@en, "Das geistige Lernen/Lehren vor dem Kontakt mit intelligenter Unendlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: we begin with the mental learn/teaching necessary for contact with intelligent infinity."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order: called necessary, without consequence."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaContactWithIntelligentInfinity ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:RaMentalDisciplines ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 94; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaBodyDisciplines a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The disciplines of the body: understanding and accepting its polarity"@en, "Die Disziplinen des Körpers: seine Polarität verstehen und annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: it is necessary to know the body well, using the mind to examine how the feelings, biases and emotions affect the various portions of the body complex, and to understand and accept the bodily polarities, repeating in a chemical/physical manifestation the work done upon the mind. The body is a creature of the mind's creation and has its biases: the biological bias must first be completely understood and then the opposite bias allowed full expression in understanding; then the body is accepted as balanced as well as polarized, and the understanding extended to the bodies of other-selves. The simplest example: each biological male is female, each biological female is male; in almost every case the most subtle discernment is necessary."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), pp. 95-96; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaBodyAcceptance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The body accepted as balanced as well as polarized"@en, "Der Körper als ausgeglichen wie auch polarisiert angenommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The acceptance of the body as a balanced as well as polarized individual, which Ra says may be accomplished once its biological bias is understood and the opposite bias given expression, and which session 6 describes as the body comfortable in whatever biases and distortions make it appropriately balanced for that instrument."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 95; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 97; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaBodyDisciplinesYieldAcceptance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The disciplines of the body yield its acceptance as balanced"@en, "Die Disziplinen des Körpers bringen seine Annahme als ausgeglichen hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the biological bias must be first completely understood and then the opposite bias allowed to find full expression in understanding; again, the process of acceptance of the body as a balanced, as well as polarized, individual may then be accomplished."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaBodyDisciplines ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaBodyAcceptance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 5 (January 23, 1981), p. 95; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 6, January 24, 1981, pp. 97-103
#

pmc:RaMindAndBodyBeforeSpirit a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind single-pointed and body comfortable before the work of the spirit"@en, "Geist einspitzig und Körper wohlauf vor dem Werk der Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the exploration and balancing of the spirit complex is the longest and most subtle part of the learn/teaching. With the mind single-pointed, balanced and aware, and the body comfortable in whatever biases make it appropriately balanced, the instrument is then ready to proceed with the greater work, the work of wind and fire. When body and mind are receptive and open, the spirit can become a functioning shuttle."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order, the last link of the chain at pmc:RaMindBeforeBody."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:RaSpiritualDiscipline ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:RaBodyDisciplines ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 97; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaSpiritualDiscipline a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The work of wind and fire: carefully and consciously opening the channel of the spirit"@en, "Das Werk von Wind und Feuer: den Kanal der Seele sorgfältig und bewusst öffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the third area is the spiritual complex, the fields of force and consciousness least distorted. The spiritual body energy field is a pathway or channel; when body and mind are receptive and open, the spirit becomes a shuttle or communicator from the entity's individual energy/will upwards and from the streamings of the creative fire and wind downwards. The purpose of carefully and consciously opening this channel is to serve in a more dependable, more commonplace way. Ra calls these exercises sufficient for the beginning and will guide further when the group feels it has accomplished what is set before it. Ra refers later to the exercise of the wind: the dissolution into nothingness is the dissolution into unity, for there is no nothingness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 97-98; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaParanormalAbilities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The healing ability and all other paranormal abilities"@en, "Die Heilfähigkeit und alle anderen paranormalen Fähigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the healing ability, like all other abilities the instrument would call paranormal, is effected by the opening of a pathway or shuttle into intelligent infinity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 97; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSpiritualDisciplineYieldsAbilities a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The careful opening of the channel yields dependable paranormal ability"@en, "Das sorgfältige Öffnen des Kanals bringt verlässliche paranormale Fähigkeit hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the purpose of carefully and consciously opening this channel is to serve in a more dependable way. To others there may appear to be miracles; to the one who has carefully opened the door to intelligent infinity this is ordinary, commonplace, as it should be. The life experience becomes somewhat transformed. The great work goes on."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the work appearing ordinary to the healer and miraculous to others, and the life experience somewhat transformed."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaSpiritualDiscipline ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaParanormalAbilities ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 97-98; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRandomGateway a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A random gateway, opened by chemicals such as LSD, taps energy without control"@en, "Ein zufälliges Tor, durch Chemikalien wie LSD geöffnet, zapft Energie ohne Kontrolle an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: there are many who have a random hole or gateway in their spirit energy field, sometimes created by the ingestion of chemicals such as LSD, who are able, randomly and without control, to tap into energy sources; they may or may not be entities who wish to serve. The purpose of carefully and consciously opening the channel is to serve in a more dependable way."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the chemical route is named with its outcome, access random and without control; the failure is put on the method of opening."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaIntelligentInfinityGateway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 97; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaThoughtFormManifestation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Travel by thought and a replica visible in third density, from the sixth"@en, "Reise durch Gedanken und ein in der dritten Dichte sichtbares Abbild, aus der sechsten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: it journeyed from Venus by thought; from the sixth dimension it is capable of manipulating by thought the intelligent infinity present in each particle of light, so that it could clothe itself in a replica, visible in the third density, of its mind/body/spirit complexes in the sixth, an experiment allowed by the Council which guards the planet. Its pyramids were thought-forms created by its social memory complex."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 84; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 98; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaCouncilOfSaturnNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Council of Saturn, which guards this planet"@en, "Der Rat des Saturn, der diesen Planeten behütet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the Council which guards this planet is located in the octave, or eighth dimension, of the planet Saturn, in the area understood in third-dimension terms as the rings. Its members are representatives from the Confederation and from the vibratory levels of the inner planes bearing responsibility for this third density; names are not part of it, though names may be offered when requested. Nine sit in constant session, varying by balancing; twenty-four further entities back them. It operates by telepathic contact with the unity of the nine and recommends action: admitting social memory complexes to the Confederation, offering aid consonant with the call, the Law and the number calling, and deciding its internal questions. A social memory complex with an idea for aid that can only be done among the people lays it before the Council; if approved, quarantine is lifted."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Council of Saturn" ;
    pm:nameRole "the council of nine guarding this planet and its quarantine, seated in the eighth dimension of Saturn" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 98-99; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 105-106; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDifficultyCommunicating a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Difficulty communicating with the instrument: her state must be deepened"@en, "Schwierigkeit, mit dem Instrument zu verkehren: ihr Zustand muss vertieft werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra, in the middle of an answer: I am having difficulty communicating with this instrument. We must deepen her state."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an observable failure in the course of a session, put on the depth of the instrument's state."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 99; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDensities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Densities, or dimensions, through which beings progress in sequence"@en, "Dichten, oder Dimensionen, durch die Wesen der Reihe nach fortschreiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins writes that Earth is near the end of the third-density cycle and that Ra, a sixth-density social memory complex, is three cycles ahead. Ra speaks of densities and dimensions interchangeably: the third density of Venus is inhospitable to this people's life-forms, its fifth and sixth dimensions conducive to learning; this sphere is now in fourth-dimension vibration, its transition disharmonious, continuing for approximately thirty years. The Confederation and the Orion group comprise entities of the third to the sixth densities. The progress through densities is sequential: a fifth-density social memory complex is comprised of mind/body/spirit complexes harvested from fourth density. Ra speaks of an octave of densities and cannot speak for those above it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 98-101; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 107-109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentAndSupportForContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "An instrument of the proper parameters, with understanding supporters, before Ra's contact"@en, "Ein Instrument der rechten Beschaffenheit, mit verständigen Unterstützern, vor Ras Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: we have searched for some of your years for an instrument of the proper parameters of distortion in mind/body/spirit complex, and for supporting and understanding mind/body/spirit complexes, to accept this information with minimal distortion and maximal desire to serve."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order in the weak sense: Ra reports a search for the condition and states no consequence of its absence; the group's desire to serve is the prior step named, with pmc:RaNonServingParticipants as its caution."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaServiceToOthers ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 101; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaQuarantine a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The quarantine of this planet and permission to break it"@en, "Die Quarantäne dieses Planeten und die Erlaubnis, sie zu brechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: each planetary entity wishing to appear within this third dimension requests permission to break quarantine; the reason is understood and accepted or rejected. As many as fifteen Confederation entities have been in the skies at one time, seven now operate craft in this density, the others being available through thought; their purpose is to let the people become aware of infinity, best expressed to the uninformed as the mysterious or unknown. The Council has not allowed the breaking of quarantine in the past thirty years; some landings are of the Orion group; permission is granted to appear in thought-form for those who have eyes to see; and permission was granted when the first nuclear device was developed and used for Confederation members to cause mystery. One landing came through quarantine in all innocence, an entity of this planet's own vibration landing at random."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 102; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 106-107; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaInstrumentStiffness a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Past the normal working time the instrument's body grows stiff"@en, "Über die gewöhnliche Arbeitszeit hinaus wird der Körper des Instruments steif"@de ;
    skos:definition "The questioner, having gone considerably over the normal working time, asks the instrument's condition; Ra: the instrument is balanced due to your care; however, her physical vehicle is growing stiff. The session is ended."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a threshold, the normal working time, exceeded, with an observable outcome, a stiff body; the failure is put on the length of the session."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 103; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 7, January 25, 1981, pp. 104-109
#

pmc:RaLawOfSquares a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of Squares: the service available is the square of the calling"@en, "Das Gesetz der Quadrate: der verfügbare Dienst ist das Quadrat des Rufes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the service available to those who call is equivalent to the square of the distortion/need of that calling, divided by or integrated with the Law of One in its distortion indicating the free will of those not aware of the unity of creation; the product is the limit of the Confederation's ability to serve. The square is sequential, one squared by the next number up to the number of callers; ten callers give approximately 1,012. Ra is called personally by 352,000 and the Confederation by 632,000,000, numbers simplified; the result is a great calling which demands its service. Coming openly among the people is reckoned not by numbers of calling but by a consensus among an entire societal-memory complex aware of the infinite consciousness of all things, possible here only in isolated instances."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the callers are sometimes not totally unified in their calling, and the squaring is then slightly less, a statistical loss over the period of the call; the failure is put on the callers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 104-105; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaCouncilOfNineNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Council of Nine, the Session Council of nine retained by two channels"@en, "Der Rat der Neun, der von zwei Kanälen bewahrte Sitzungsrat der Neun"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether the nine of the Council are the nine of Puharich's book, Ra says the Council of Nine has been retained in semi-undistorted form by two main sources, Mark Probert and Henry Puharich; in one case the channel became the scribe, in the other the channel was not the scribe, but without the aid of the scribe the energy would not have come to the channel."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Council of Nine" ;
    pm:nameRole "the nine who sit in constant session in the Council of Saturn, contacted through human channels" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 106; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaGuardiansNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Guardians, the twenty-four who back the Council"@en, "Die Wächter, die vierundzwanzig, die den Rat stützen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: to back the Council of nine there are twenty-four entities which offer their services as requested; these entities faithfully watch and have been called Guardians; the Council may contact them when in doubt for consensus and judgment, and then reconsider any question."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Guardians" ;
    pm:nameRole "twenty-four entities who watch and advise the Council of Saturn" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 106; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaScribeRole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The scribe, without whose aid the energy would not have come to the channel"@en, "Der Schreiber, ohne dessen Hilfe die Energie nicht zum Kanal gekommen wäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra on the two channels of the Council of Nine: in one case the channel became the scribe; in the other the channel was not the scribe; however, without the aid of the scribe the energy would not have come to the channel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 106; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaScribeBeforeReception a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The scribe's aid before the energy reaches the channel"@en, "Die Hilfe des Schreibers, bevor die Energie den Kanal erreicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: without the aid of the scribe, the energy would not have come to the channel."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the absence of the scribe is named as a reason the channel would receive nothing; the failure is put on the composition of the group."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaScribeRole ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without the aid of the scribe, the energy would not have come to the channel (session 7, p. 106)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 106; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAwarenessOfInfinity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of infinite possibility, roused by mystery"@en, "Gewahrsein unendlicher Möglichkeit, durch das Geheimnis geweckt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The awareness of infinity, which Ra says is often best expressed to the uninformed as the mysterious or unknown, and which the Confederation's appearances are meant to arouse: the mystery and unknown quality of the occurrences it is allowed to offer has the intention of making the people aware of infinite possibility. The advertisement is general, not designed to indicate any particular material but only to suggest the noumenal aspect of the illusion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 102; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 107; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaGraspingInfinityBeforeGateway a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Infinity grasped before the gateway to the Law of One can be opened"@en, "Unendlichkeit erfasst, bevor das Tor zum Gesetz des Einen geöffnet werden kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: when your peoples grasp infinity, then and only then, can the gateway be opened to the Law of One."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: then and only then: without the grasp of infinity the gateway stays shut; the failure is put on the people's awareness and is not observable."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaIntelligentInfinityGateway ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaAwarenessOfInfinity ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Only when the people grasp infinity can the gateway be opened to the Law of One; then and only then (session 7, p. 107)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 107; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaOrionGroupNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Orion group, which calls itself to conquest"@en, "Die Orion-Gruppe, die sich selbst zur Eroberung ruft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: some of the landings at this time are of the entities known as the group of Orion. Its intention is presumably to unify by choosing the elite from a social memory complex and enslaving by various effects those seen as not elite, and to add the social memory complex thus weeded to what it thinks of as an empire; its purpose is conquest, unlike the Confederation, which waits for the calling. It comprises a very few third-density, larger numbers of fourth- and fifth-density and very few sixth-density entities, perhaps one-tenth the Confederation's number; its power is the same."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Orion group" ;
    pm:nameRole "a group of social memory complexes of the third to sixth densities oriented to service to self, seeking conquest" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 107-108; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaServiceToSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Service to self: seeking intelligent infinity through power over others"@en, "Dienst am Selbst: die intelligente Unendlichkeit durch Macht über andere suchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the Law of One blinks neither at the light nor the darkness but is available for service to others and service to self. Those seeking intelligent infinity through service to self create the same amount of power, but have constant difficulty because of the concept of separation implicit in the power over others. Those who found light/love without a desire for service to others have by the Law of Free Will the right to use it for whatever purpose, and there are systems of study that enable the seeker of separation to gain the gateways. Those who seek to serve the self are seen by the Law of One as precisely the same as those who seek to serve others, for are all not one; to serve yourself and to serve others is a dual method of saying the same thing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 107-109; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSpiritualEntropy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual entropy: the disintegration of social memory complexes founded on separation"@en, "Geistige Entropie: der Zerfall sozialer Gedächtniskomplexe, die auf Trennung gründen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the Orion group faces a great deal of random energy released by the concept of separation, which makes it vulnerable because the distortions among its own members are not harmonized; the problem of spiritual entropy causes it to experience constant disintegration of its social memory complexes. The separation implicit in power over others weakens and eventually disintegrates the energy collected by those who call the Orion group and by the complexes which comprise it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: separation is named as the cause of the weakening and disintegration of the energy of the path of service to self; the outcome is stated as constant, and the failure is put on the orientation itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 107-108; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaServiceToSelfStudy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Systems of study by which the seeker of separation gains the gateways"@en, "Lehrwege, durch die der Sucher der Trennung die Tore gewinnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: there are systems of study which enable the seeker of separation to gain these gateways; this study is as difficult as the one described to the group, but there are those with the perseverance to pursue it, as the questioner desires to pursue the difficult path of seeking to know in order to serve."@en ;
    skos:note "The systems are named as existing and not described."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaServiceToSelfStudyYieldsGateway a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The study of separation yields the gateway to intelligent infinity"@en, "Das Studium der Trennung bringt das Tor zur intelligenten Unendlichkeit hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: those not oriented toward service to others nevertheless find and can use the gateway to intelligent infinity, at all densities of this octave; systems of study enable the seeker of separation to gain these gateways."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaServiceToSelfStudy ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaIntelligentInfinityGateway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 108-109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHarvestability a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Harvestability: seeing and enjoying the light/love of the next density"@en, "Erntefähigkeit: das Licht/die Liebe der nächsten Dichte sehen und genießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra: the beings are harvested because they can see and enjoy the light/love of the appropriate density, and this holds for those who found it without desire for service to others as well. The spirit complex of each harvested entity moves along the line of light until the light grows too glaring, and there stops."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), p. 100; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSocialMemoryComplex a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The social memory complex: a group consciousness of one understanding"@en, "Der soziale Gedächtniskomplex: ein Gruppenbewusstsein eines Verständnisses"@de ;
    skos:definition "The form of being Ra gives for itself, for the members of the Confederation and of the Orion group: a group, or what this people would call a social memory complex, sharing understanding. Ra says the mass mind of such a complex, its members each containing an acceptable distortion, could move mountains; a fifth-density social memory complex is comprised of entities harvested from fourth density and then melded; the Law of One is available to any social memory complex that has decided to strive together for any purpose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 71; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), p. 84; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), pp. 107-108; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

#
# Session 8, January 26, 1981, pp. 110-112
#

pmc:RaOpportunityEachNeeds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each entity receives the opportunity it needs"@en, "Jedes Wesen erhält die Gelegenheit, die es braucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether the material could be advertised, Ra asks the questioner to consider the path his life has taken, the coincidences and odd circumstances by which one thing flowed to the next, and says each entity will receive the opportunity that each needs; this information is not of use in the life of each who seeks, so the advertisement is general."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPreIncarnativeResolve a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The resolve before incarnation to be of service, without which the contactee would not have been used"@en, "Der Entschluss vor der Inkarnation, zu dienen, ohne den der Kontaktierte nicht gebraucht worden wäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra on the Pascagoula case of 1973: the entities who took Charlie Hixson aboard, third-density beings of a fairly advanced order from Sirius, came through quarantine at random and used his life experience, concentrating on his experience of war, to learn of the Law of One, as a race watches a film; they would not have used him except for the resolve of this entity before incarnation to be of service."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: without the resolve before incarnation the contact would not have taken place; the failure is put on the contactee's choice before birth and is not observable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), pp. 110-111; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDirectContactRefusal a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ra backs off from direct contact in thought-form and declines to take anyone aboard"@en, "Ra zieht sich vom unmittelbaren Kontakt in Gedankenform zurück und lehnt ab, jemanden an Bord zu nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra, asked whether any of the group could have more direct contact with the Confederation: in observing the distortions of those who underwent this experiential sequence, it decided to back off gradually from direct contact in thought-form. The least distortion seems to be available in mind-to-mind communication; therefore the request to be taken aboard is not one it cares to comply with; the group is most valuable in its present orientation. Ra adds that, had it arrived in no other form than its own, it would have been perceived as light."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: Ra names the distortions observed in those who underwent direct contact as the reason to withdraw from it; the failure is put on the contactees and the mode of contact."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaConfederation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), pp. 111-112; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

